{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01S4WSQTSrKRUW6S4Phxqfy1","type":"tool_result","content":"18:- Further moves, on request: `new E.Platformer({ crouch: true, ledge: true, wallCling: true, momentum: true })`; tiles of `kind: 'water' | 'rope' | 'bars'`, and grip on any tile type: `friction` (ice: .15), `carry` (a conveyor's speed), `bounce` (a spring), `crumble` with `respawn` (call `level.update(dt)` each step); `hero.swingFrom(x, z)` hangs it from a grapple point. Draw `level.drawWater(r)` after the actors; `rigState()` poses every move (hang, climb, crawl, swim, swing).\n39:- `E.Match` runs the rounds, the clock, KO and time over, the calls and the HUD; `E.FightAI({ level, seed })` is a CPU whose matches repeat with its seed; `E.FightSelect` is the character select; `training: { dummy }` draws the boxes, the frame data and the inputs. Update the match once a step (motions are read at 120 Hz) and draw the stage before `match.draw(r)`.\n47:- Bosses fire `E.pattern.ring` and `spread`, each attack telegraphed. A bomb clears `shots.clear('foe')`. The end: `E.Arcade`'s continue, then initials and the table (the arcade module).\n49:**Golden-age arcade (Pac-Man, Galaga, Asteroids).** Start from the ARCADE slice: a cabinet of three.\n51:- `new E.Arcade(game, { id, lives: 3, extra: [10000] })` keeps the score, lives, two players' turns (each one's stage in `p.save`), the continue, the tables with initials and the attract mode; `cab.update(dt)` each step and `cab.draw(r, box)` after the game.\n55:**Kart racing (Super Mario Kart, F-Zero).** Start from the KART slice (the mode7 and drive modules).\n56:- The track is a TileMap: its walls bounce the karts, its floor tags (`grass`, `sand`, `boost`, ...) slow or boost them (`E.Car`'s `surfaces`), and `E.Mode7({ floor: (x, y) => [r, g, b] })` draws it from the same cells. The racing line is a closed `E.Path` through the track's middle: `E.Race({ path, laps: 3 })` counts laps through its checkpoints in order (a shortcut counts nothing), gives places, and drives every car not a player's (`race.add(car, { input })` for a player, `{ ai: { skill } }` for the rest).\n57:- Each step `race.update(dt, map)` (it moves every car), then the camera behind yours, turning after it more slowly than the kart turns (a drift shows): `m7.cam = cam; m7.chase({ x, y, angle: camAngle }, { back: 42, h: 24 })`. Draw the karts with `m7.add(x, y, z, (g, sx, sy, k) => ...)`: a few boxes through `m7.view(k)`'s projection and the rig seated (`down: .4`) in the middle, sorted far to near from the camera's side.\n58:- Two players: `game.allowJoin({ max: 2 })`, `game.splitScreen(2, { layout: 'rows' })`, and in `draw` each viewport its own camera: `m7.draw(r, cams[r.viewport.i])`, `race.hud(r, players[r.viewport.i])`. On a phone the gas goes on by itself (`car.o.auto`), the stick steers, DRIFT and ITEM are buttons; held upright, draw from further back with a wider field of view.\n60:**Road racing (OutRun, Pole Position, Hang-On).** Start from the ROAD slice (the road module).\n61:- `E.Road` is the course: `road.add(n, { curve, hill, tunnel, colors })` stretch by stretch; scenery with `road.place(z, offset, sprite, scale)` (`E.prop('palm').frames[0]` works), traffic as `cars: [{ z, x, w, draw }]` passed to `road.draw`. The player is a position (`z` along, `x` across in half roads) and a speed, not a body.\n62:- Each step: `x -= road.curveAt(z) * speed² * k` throws the car outward on a bend (make the hardest faster than the player can steer: they slow down), off the road (`|x| > 1`) it slows, `road.hits(z, x, w)` crashes it into the scenery (put it back on the road), and a car close in `z` and `x` bumps it. A clock that counts down and checkpoints that add time make the race.\n64:**Top-down racing and driving (Micro Machines, RC Pro-Am, GTA).** `E.Car` on a TileMap in the `topdown` view: the same cars, laps and drivers as the kart (`E.Race`), drawn from above (a box of `px.poly` on `r.w()` corner points, turned by `car.angle`); GTA's car is a `E.Car` the hero gets into (`kart: false`: drift is a handbrake).\n71:- Saves: `game.saves` (the party's `state()`, the story's `state()`, the map and the place); a crystal to save at, the inn's autosave, Continue and Load on the title. The menu's windows are `rpg.list` and `rpg.card`, rows a thumb's height on a phone.\n107:- Guests carry money and `needs` (fun, hunger, thirst, tired) that `E.needs` raises each step; `E.choose(guest, options)` takes the ride or shop that serves them best for the walk and the price (an option's `gives: { fun: -.5 }`, its door's x, y, its cost). They queue, ride, pay, think aloud (\"THIS LINE IS TOO LONG\"), and leave when tired, broke or at closing; the rating is how happy they leave.\n109:- Moving rides are shapes too: a generator's `params` (an angle in 16 or 24 steps) or `facing` (32 steps) each make a still picture, kept, so a turning carousel costs what a still one does.\n111:**3D-era remake (Mario 64, Ocarina, Crash).**\n137:- Lemmings: an `E.Terrain` level (a picture's cells as materials), each lemming a walker (`land.walk`: a step up of 5, a fall that kills past a landing speed), diggers and bashers carving a small circle or a polygon each step, builders adding a short bar (`addPoly`); hundreds of walkers are cheap (no physics bodies).\n148:- Soldiers are walkers (`land.walk`): its landing speed past a limit is fall damage; under the water line they drown. A blast `land.carve`s, hurts each one by its distance and throws it (`vx`, `vy`, `ground = false`).\n163:**3D kart racing (Mario Kart 64, Crash Team Racing).** The 3D RACING kit (the drive module). The circuit is a `world.track` along a closed `E.Path` with heights (banked bends, a hill, a hump to jump, boost `pads`, `gaps` in its walls where a shortcut, a track of its own with `surface: 'dirt'`, leaves and rejoins); karts are `world.vehicle({ kind: 'kart', rig })` raced by `E.Race` (`race.update(dt, null)`: laps, places, its drivers, items); the camera `'behind'` each; set a kart that has left the course back on the road after a moment (Lakitu); two players through `game.splitScreen(2)` and `world.addCamera`.\n176:- Waves spawn from the room's edges by a timeline; grunts walk straight at the hero, others wander, hulks can't be killed, humans to rescue for points. `cam.shake` and `game.freeze(.03)` on every kill keep it loud; `E.Arcade` keeps the score, the lives and the table.\n178:**Bomberman.** Start from the PUZZLE slice's grid or the ARCADE's maze (the grid module).\n187:**Frogger.** An `E.Grid` of lanes in `overhead`: the frog an `E.GridMover` that hops a cell per press; each lane a row of cars or logs moving at its own speed (`x += v * dt`, wrapping at the screen's edge). On a road a car's box kills; on the river the frog rides a log (add its speed) and drowns off one. Five homes at the top; a clock bar per life.\n191:**Sonic without the loops (Sonic the Hedgehog's speed on flat ground and slopes).** Start from the PLATFORMER slice: `new E.Platformer({ momentum: true })` (speed builds up and carries, slowing on the way up a slope and gathering on the way down: tiles of `kind: 'slope'`), a roll on down at speed, rings that scatter when hit (`E.Bullets` fired with `grav`) and are lost after a while, springs and long camera leads (`game.follow(hero, { lead: 60 })`). Loops and walls run round need a ground of any angle the Platformer doesn't have: leave them out.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a6a22e8e-f9ad-4c1e-b19f-6f268b0ad619","uuid":"9477b406-135d-4fa5-8a4b-c088fd09ea8d","timestamp":"2026-11-04T00:55:33.764Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"18:- Further moves, on request: `new E.Platformer({ crouch: true, ledge: true, wallCling: true, momentum: true })`; tiles of `kind: 'water' | 'rope' | 'bars'`, and grip on any tile type: `friction` (ice: .15), `carry` (a conveyor's speed), `bounce` (a spring), `crumble` with `respawn` (call `level.update(dt)` e