{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01ARqUL1o6J2WZk9w2HAZDYG","type":"tool_result","content":"15:- In draw: m7.rig(rig, x, y, z), m7.sprite(spr or E.anim, x, y, z, { scale, flip, t }), m7.shape(id, x, y, z, { facing,\n21:  view(k) (the engine view a rig is drawn with at k).\n91:  rig(rig, x, y, z = 0) { return this.add(x, y, z, (g, sx, sy, k) => rig.draw(g, Math.round(sx), Math.round(sy), this.view(k))); }\n102:  shape(id, x, y, z = 0, o = {}) {\n104:      const v = this.view(k), f = Math.round((o.facing === undefined ? Math.PI / 2 : o.facing) / Math.PI * 8) / 8 * Math.PI, key = id + ':' + v.scale + ':' + v.yawDeg + ':' + v.pitchDeg + ':' + f + ':' + (o.size || 1);\n110:  view(k) {\n21:  view(k) (the engine view a rig is drawn with at k).\n91:  rig(rig, x, y, z = 0) { return this.add(x, y, z, (g, sx, sy, k) => rig.draw(g, Math.round(sx), Math.round(sy), this.view(k))); }\n110:  view(k) {\n- m7.project(x, y, z) -> [sx, sy, k] on the screen, or null behind the camera; m7.toFloor(sx, sy) -> [x, y], or null\n  above the horizon (both for the camera last drawn: HUD markers, a tap on the track). m7.horizon: its screen row.\n- Your own pass: m7.begin({ W, H, x, y, cx, cy, focal }, cam), then project, rowDepth(sy), drawFloor(g, rect),\n  view(k) (the engine view a rig is drawn with at k).\n- Resolution: the game's own pixels by default, as the SNES drew; m7.fullRes(game, true) each step draws at the\n  screen's own (sharper, slower; it returns the pixel size the game had), false gives the game's pixels back.\n\n```js mode7\nconst E = My3D2dge, m7 = new E.Mode7({ floor: (x, y) => ((x >> 4) + (y >> 4)) & 1 ? [80, 160, 80] : [60, 130, 60], size: [512, 512] });\nm7.cam = { x: 256, y: 400, h: 40, angle: -Math.PI / 2, pitch: 12, fov: 70 };\nm7.begin({ W: 320, H: 240 });\nconst p = m7.project(256, 300, 0), q = m7.toFloor(p[0], p[1]);\nif (Math.abs(q[0] - 256) > .01 || Math.abs(q[1] - 300) > .01 || p[1] <= m7.horizon) throw new Error('a floor point and back');\n```\nRules: m7.draw covers its viewport (draw nothing under it you need to see); move the camera in update, not draw; a\nbody's angle and the camera's heading are the same angle; billboards are gathered again every frame.\n*/\n(function (E) {\n'use strict';\nif (!E) throw new Error('my-3D2dge module MODE7: load engine/my-3d2dge.js (or the agent edition) first');\n\n/* =============================================================================\n * MODE 7  a perspective floor a row at a time, its sky, billboards scaled by distance\n * ========================================================================== */\nconst { clamp } = E;\n// cos and sin, exact at the quarter turns (a camera looking due north projects as the stress test always did)\nconst trig = a => { let c = Math.cos(a), s = Math.sin(a); if (Math.abs(c) < 1e-12) c = 0; if (Math.abs(s) < 1e-12) s = 0; return [c, s]; };\nclass Mode7 {\n  /** new E.Mode7({ floor, size, outside, wrap, sky, fog, far }): a Mode 7 view (the manual above) */\n  constructor(o = {}) {\n    /** o: its options */\n    this.o = Object.assign({ outside: '#24402a', far: 2400, sky: ['#1a3060', '#7aa8e0'] }, o);\n    /** cam: the camera ({ x, y, h, angle, pitch, fov }); horizon: the screen row of the horizon in the last drawing;\n     *  items: the billboards gathered for the next draw */","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a6a22e8e-f9ad-4c1e-b19f-6f268b0ad619","uuid":"f6ce3f1e-d857-433f-b5aa-dd6db1471e40","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:00:14.864Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"15:- In draw: m7.rig(rig, x, y, z), m7.sprite(spr or E.anim, x, y, z, { scale, flip, t }), m7.shape(id, x, y, z, { facing,\n21:  view(k) (the engine view a rig is drawn with at k).\n91:  rig(rig, x, y, z = 0) { return this.add(x, y, z, (g, sx, sy, k) => rig.draw(g, Math.round(sx), Math.round(sy), this.view(k))); }\n102:  shape(id, x, y, z = 0, o = {}) {\n104:      const v = this.view(k), f = Math.round((o.facing === undefined ? Math.PI / 2 : o.facing) / Math.PI * 8) / 8 * Math.PI, key = id + ':' + v.scale + ':' + v.yawDeg + ':' + v.pitchDeg + ':' + f + ':' + (o.size || 1);\n110:  view(k) {\n21:  view(k) (the engine view a rig is drawn with at k).\n91:  rig(rig, x, y, z = 0) { return this.add(x, y, z, (g, sx, sy, k) => rig.draw(g, Math.round(sx), Math.round(sy), this.view(k))); }\n110:  view(k) {\n- m7.project(x, y, z) -> [sx, sy, k] on the screen, or null behind the camera; m7.toFloor(sx, sy) -> [x, y], or null\n  above the horizon (both for the camera last drawn: HUD markers, a tap on the track). m7.horizon: its screen row.\n- Your own pass: m7.begin({ W, H, x, y, cx, cy, focal }, cam), then project, rowDepth(sy), drawFloor(g, rect),\n  view(k) (the engine view a rig is drawn with at k).\n- Resolution: the game's own pixels by default, as the SNES drew; m7.fullRes(game, true) each step draws at the\n  screen's own (sharper, slower; it returns the pixel size the game had), false gives the game's pixels back.\n\n```js mode7\nconst E = My3D2dge, m7 = new E.Mode7({ floor: (x, y) => ((x >> 4) + (y >> 4)) & 1 ? [80, 160, 80] : [60, 130, 60], size: [512, 512] });\nm7.cam = { x: 256, y: 400, h: 40, angle: -Math.PI / 2, pitch: 12, fov: 70 };\nm7.begin({ W: 320, H: 240 });\nconst p = m7.project(256, 300, 0), q = m7.toFloor(p[0], p[1]);\nif (Math.abs(q[0] - 256) > .01 || Math.abs(q[1] - 300) > .01 || p[1] <= m7.horizon) throw new Error('a floor point and back');\n```\nRules: m7.draw covers its viewport (draw nothing under it you need to see); move the camera in update, not draw; a\nbody's angle and the camera's heading are the same angle; billboards are gathered again every frame.\n*/\n(function (E) {\n'use strict';\nif (!E) throw new Error('my-3D2dge module MODE7: load engine/my-3d2dge.js (or the agent edition) first');\n\n/* =============================================================================\n * MODE 7  a perspective floor a row at a time, its sky, billboards scaled by distance\n * ========================================================================== */\nconst { clamp } = E;\n// cos and sin, exact at the quarter turns (a camera looking due north projects as the stress test always did)\nconst trig = a => { let c = Math.cos(a), s = Math.sin(a); if (Math.abs(c) < 1e-12) c = 0; if (Math.abs(s) < 1e-12) s = 0; return [c, s]; };\nclass Mode7 {\n  /** new E.Mode7({ floor, size, outside, wrap, sky, fog, far }): a Mode 7 view (the manual above) */\n  constructor(o = {}) {\n    /** o: its options */\n    this.o = Object.assign({ outside: '#24402a', far: 2400, sky: ['#1a3060', '#7aa8e0'] }, o);\n    /** cam: the camera ({ x, y, h, angle, pitch, fov }); horizon: the screen row of the horizon in the last drawing;\n     *  items: the billboards gathered for the next draw */","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01ARqUL1o6J2WZk9w2HAZDYG","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CggyyjXgfnEEitZDDyFRm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01NajsAYFhf8SyHupymLk1g4","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"H=/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174801__xc8e150/work/_research/my-3d2dge/dist/handoff; sed -n 100,125p $H/modules/mode7.js | cut -c1-600","description":"Read mode7's view(k) and shape billboard code"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1797,"cache_read_input_tokens":212662,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1797},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a6a22e8e-f9ad-4c1e-b19f-6f268b0ad619","uuid":"34b97815-6eb3-4803-a393-33c5411c11e5","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:00:19.133Z","request_id":"req_011CggyyjHJFfJd587qQAnkp","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01NajsAYFhf8SyHupymLk1g4":{"command":"H=/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174801__xc8e150/work/_research/my-3d2dge/dist/handoff; sed -n 100,125p $H/modules/mode7.js | cut -c1-600","description":"Read mode7's view(k) and shape billboard code"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NajsAYFhf8SyHupymLk1g4","type":"tool_result","content":"  /** gather one of the engine's shapes (r.shape's: 'barrel', 'tree', ...; the full engine), seen from the camera's side at\n   *  its distance's size: o.facing (radians), o.size (1) */\n  shape(id, x, y, z = 0, o = {}) {\n    return this.add(x, y, z, (g, sx, sy, k) => {\n      const v = this.view(k), f = Math.round((o.facing === undefined ? Math.PI / 2 : o.facing) / Math.PI * 8) / 8 * Math.PI, key = id + ':' + v.scale + ':' + v.yawDeg + ':' + v.pitchDeg + ':' + f + ':' + (o.size || 1);\n      let sp = this._shapes.get(key); if (sp === undefined) { if (this._shapes.size > 300) this._shapes.clear(); sp = E.shapeSprite ? E.shapeSprite(id, { view: v, facing: f, size: o.size || 1 }) : null; this._shapes.set(key, sp); }\n      if (sp) g.drawImage(sp.cv, Math.round(sx - sp.foot[0]), Math.round(sy - sp.foot[1]));\n    });\n  }\n  /** the engine view a rig is drawn with at k pixels per unit, seen from the camera's heading (sixteenths, reused) */\n  view(k) {\n    const q = Math.max(1 / 8, Math.round(k * 16) / 16), yaw = (Math.round((-this._a * 180 / Math.PI - 90) * 2) / 2) || 0, key = q + ':' + yaw + ':' + this._pd;\n    let v = this._views.get(key); if (!v) { if (this._views.size > 400) this._views.clear(); v = new E.View('mode7', 'Mode 7', yaw, this._pd, q, 1); this._views.set(key, v); }\n    return v;\n  }\n  /** draw the view as an overlay over r's frame (in a split screen, r.viewport's part): sky, floor, fog, then the\n   *  billboards far to near (gathered with add, rig, sprite; they are used up) */\n  draw(r, cam = this.cam) {\n    const vp = r.viewport || { x: 0, y: 0, w: r.bw, h: r.bh }, items = this.items.splice(0), sc = r.game.screen, whole = !r.viewport;\n    r.overlay(g => {\n      this.begin({ W: whole ? r.W : vp.w, H: whole ? r.H : vp.h, x: vp.x, y: vp.y, cx: whole ? r.W / 2 + sc.fx : vp.x + vp.w / 2, cy: whole ? r.H / 2 + sc.fy : vp.y + vp.h / 2 }, cam);\n      this._t = r.game.time;\n      // drawn on a canvas of the viewport's size (moved so screen points land on it), then onto the frame\n      const c = this._out && this._out.width === vp.w && this._out.height === vp.h ? this._out : (this._out = E.mkCanvas(vp.w, vp.h)), cg = E.ctx2d(c);\n      cg.setTransform(1, 0, 0, 1, -vp.x, -vp.y);\n      this.drawSky(cg, r, vp); this.drawFloor(cg, vp);","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a6a22e8e-f9ad-4c1e-b19f-6f268b0ad619","uuid":"5e0099ca-706f-450e-87bf-93874219ccf7","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:00:19.157Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"  /** gather one of the engine's shapes (r.shape's: 'barrel', 'tree', ...; the full engine), seen from the camera's side at\n   *  its distance's size: o.facing (radians), o.size (1) */\n  shape(id, x, y, z = 0, o = {}) {\n    return this.add(x, y, z, (g, sx, sy, k) => {\n      const v = this.view(k), f = Math.round((o.facing === undefined ? Math.PI / 2 : o.facing) / Math.PI * 8) / 8 * Math.PI, key = id + ':' + v.scale + ':' + v.yawDeg + ':' + v.pitchDeg + ':' + f + ':' + (o.size || 1);\n      let sp = this._shapes.get(key); if (sp === undefined) { if (this._shapes.size > 300) this._shapes.clear(); sp = E.shapeSprite ? E.shapeSprite(id, { view: v, facing: f, size: o.size || 1 }) : null; this._shapes.set(key, sp); }\n      if (sp) g.drawImage(sp.cv, Math.round(sx - sp.foot[0]), Math.round(sy - sp.foot[1]));\n    });\n  }\n  /** the engine view a rig is drawn with at k pixels per unit, seen from the camera's heading (sixteenths, reused) */\n  view(k) {\n    const q = Math.max(1 / 8, Math.round(k * 16) / 16), yaw = (Math.round((-this._a * 180 / Math.PI - 90) * 2) / 2) || 0, key = q + ':' + yaw + ':' + this._pd;\n    let v = this._views.get(key); if (!v) { if (this._views.size > 400) this._views.clear(); v = new E.View('mode7', 'Mode 7', yaw, this._pd, q, 1); this._views.set(key, v); }\n    return v;\n  }\n  /** draw the view as an overlay over r's frame (in a split screen, r.viewport's part): sky, floor, fog, then the\n   *  billboards far to near (gathered with add, rig, sprite; they are used up) */\n  draw(r, cam = this.cam) {\n    const vp = r.viewport || { x: 0, y: 0, w: r.bw, h: r.bh }, items = this.items.splice(0), sc = r.game.screen, whole = !r.viewport;\n    r.overlay(g => {\n      this.begin({ W: whole ? r.W : vp.w, H: whole ? r.H : vp.h, x: vp.x, y: vp.y, cx: whole ? r.W / 2 + sc.fx : vp.x + vp.w / 2, cy: whole ? r.H / 2 + sc.fy : vp.y + vp.h / 2 }, cam);\n      this._t = r.game.time;\n      // drawn on a canvas of the viewport's size (moved so screen points land on it), then onto the frame\n      const c = this._out && this._out.width === vp.w && this._out.height === vp.h ? this._out : (this._out = E.mkCanvas(vp.w, vp.h)), cg = E.ctx2d(c);\n      cg.setTransform(1, 0, 0, 1, -vp.x, -vp.y);\n      this.drawSky(cg, r, vp); this.drawFloor(cg, vp);","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01NajsAYFhf8SyHupymLk1g4","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
