{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017WuVeA4ErCDCfztLPbWGJD","type":"tool_result","content":"289:- `input.feed(type, x, y, o = {})` †: a pointer event in screen pixels, as the browser's would give: feed('down' | 'move' | 'up', x, y, { touch: false, button: 0, id: 0 (which finger, for zones) }) (a test's or a bot's mouse and fingers: clicks, boxes, long presses, double taps and pans follow; \n501:- `game.splitScreen(n, o = {})` †: split the screen into n viewports (2 to 4; 0 or 1: one screen again), o: { layout: 'auto' (side by side on a wide screen, stacked on a tall one; a grid for 3 or 4) | 'columns' | 'rows' | 'grid', follow: [targets], z: 16, gap: 1 }\n510:- `game.viewports` †: a split screen's viewports ({ i, x, y, w, h, cam, focus(x, y, z), follow(target, { z }): game.splitScreen), or [] on one screen\n303:- `input.rebindable(a, map = this.preset)` †: can the player rebind action a? Every action but the menu's (start, pause, confirm, cancel: they are how a player gets back to the menu), and those the game hides with new E.Game({ menu: { controls: { a: false } } })\n484:- `game.menu(name)`: open the menu (the corner's menu button and the touch START do it): a pausable scene (or a game started without scenes) pauses on its pause screen; any other scene, a title, waits under the settings. menu('settings') or menu('controls') opens that screen. Without a menu (men\n489:- `game.pause(reason = 'player')`: pause the game, saying why ('player' | 'focus' | 'controller' | 'menu': pauseReason); returns true if it paused. The player resumes (Escape, Start, Resume); resume() does it from code\n1081:- `new E.Backdrop(o = {}) → backdrop`: new E.Backdrop('castle-night') (a preset: E.Backdrop.presets) or new E.Backdrop({ sky: [colors top to bottom], sun, moon, stars, layers: [{ kind: 'mountains' | 'hills' | 'forest' | 'city' | 'castle' | 'clouds' | 'sea' | 'fog' | 'stalactites', color, y, height, parallax, seed }] }): a parallax sky and scenery drawn behind a level. sun, moon: { x, y (0..1 of the screen), r, color }","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a6a22e8e-f9ad-4c1e-b19f-6f268b0ad619","uuid":"394704ed-92be-4264-b192-bbe8e025095e","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:01:44.823Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"289:- `input.feed(type, x, y, o = {})` †: a pointer event in screen pixels, as the browser's would give: feed('down' | 'move' | 'up', x, y, { touch: false, button: 0, id: 0 (which finger, for zones) }) (a test's or a bot's mouse and fingers: clicks, boxes, long presses, double taps and pans follow; \n501:- `game.splitScreen(n, o = {})` †: split the screen into n viewports (2 to 4; 0 or 1: one screen again), o: { layout: 'auto' (side by side on a wide screen, stacked on a tall one; a grid for 3 or 4) | 'columns' | 'rows' | 'grid', follow: [targets], z: 16, gap: 1 }\n510:- `game.viewports` †: a split screen's viewports ({ i, x, y, w, h, cam, focus(x, y, z), follow(target, { z }): game.splitScreen), or [] on one screen\n303:- `input.rebindable(a, map = this.preset)` †: can the player rebind action a? Every action but the menu's (start, pause, confirm, cancel: they are how a player gets back to the menu), and those the game hides with new E.Game({ menu: { controls: { a: false } } })\n484:- `game.menu(name)`: open the menu (the corner's menu button and the touch START do it): a pausable scene (or a game started without scenes) pauses on its pause screen; any other scene, a title, waits under the settings. menu('settings') or menu('controls') opens that screen. Without a menu (men\n489:- `game.pause(reason = 'player')`: pause the game, saying why ('player' | 'focus' | 'controller' | 'menu': pauseReason); returns true if it paused. The player resumes (Escape, Start, Resume); resume() does it from code\n1081:- `new E.Backdrop(o = {}) → backdrop`: new E.Backdrop('castle-night') (a preset: E.Backdrop.presets) or new E.Backdrop({ sky: [colors top to bottom], sun, moon, stars, layers: [{ kind: 'mountains' | 'hills' | 'forest' | 'city' | 'castle' | 'clouds' | 'sea' | 'fog' | 'stalactites', color, y, height, parallax, seed }] }): a parallax sky and scenery drawn behind a level. sun, moon: { x, y (0..1 of the screen), r, color }","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_017WuVeA4ErCDCfztLPbWGJD","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
