{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgh2UqCXiv1drYqtZMvWS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01FPCdGNLp3GWP3LMMKxAkPD","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174801__xc8e150/work/PLAN.md","offset":140,"limit":200},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5166,"cache_read_input_tokens":411824,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5166},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a6a22e8e-f9ad-4c1e-b19f-6f268b0ad619","uuid":"a5179796-85c5-474f-ba4a-4715dbe4846a","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:33:08.941Z","request_id":"req_011Cgh2UpkzSXj1hi3gy2yBK","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01FPCdGNLp3GWP3LMMKxAkPD":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174801__xc8e150/work/PLAN.md","offset":140,"limit":200}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FPCdGNLp3GWP3LMMKxAkPD","type":"tool_result","content":"140\t  - P2: ↑/↓ lever, `.` call, `/` horn, `,` ATS, L EB, `;` neutral, `'` view.\n141\t  - Show these on the Duel lobby screen.\n142\t\n143\t---\n144\t\n145\t## 3. Architecture\n146\t\n147\t### 3.1 Stack and why\n148\t\n149\t- **my-3D2dge v0.85.2, full engine** (`my-3d2dge.js` from the handoff package). It includes every module, the HTML Shell (pause, settings, controls),\n150\t  Menus, Dialog with portraits, Humanoid and Blob rigs, the chip synth, input with glyph labels and rumble, split screen, boot steps, store and\n151\t  saves, and the headless `game.advance` / `game.debug` testing.\n152\t  - Use the 2D engine only. The three.js 3D engine is not in the handoff package, it runs poorly headless, and its look isn't the engine's\n153\t    native pixel style.\n154\t- **New module `rail.js`**, our pseudo-3D railway renderer. It is a fork of `modules/road.js` (OutRun-style segments) extended for tracks, platforms,\n155\t  trains and rear-facing cameras (§4.1). This is the heart of the game's look.\n156\t- **AI Hub client `session.js` 1.4.0**, pasted unmodified as the first script in `<head>`, right after `<meta charset>`.\n157\t- **No other libraries and no CDN.** The single HTML inlines everything, so it runs offline from `file://`.\n158\t- **Tooling:** Node 18+; Playwright 1.63.0 (as pinned in the handoff `package.json`; reuse an installed Chromium if one is there); python3\n159\t  `http.server` for the hub harness only.\n160\t- **Resolution:** `res: 'ps1', expand: true` gives 320×240 as a minimum and about 427×240 on 16:9. Anchor all HUD to `r.W`/`r.H`.\n161\t\n162\t### 3.2 Dev folder layout\n163\t\n164\t```\n165\tDenshaDeHalo-DenshaDeGo-<model>-<ts>/\n166\t  engine/                  copy of dist/handoff (my-3d2dge.js patched per §3.8, tools/, docs/, package.json, kits/ for reference)\n167\t  engine/modules/rail.js   NEW: the rail renderer (§4.1), loaded after my-3d2dge.js\n168\t  vendor/aihub/            session.js (unmodified), harness.html, bridge.js, round.js (harness files are for tests only, never bundled)\n169\t  src/                     the game, in load order (each file one IIFE writing only into the DH namespace):\n170\t    00-core.js             DH namespace, E, the E.Game, constants, units, DH.rng, settings definitions, input map (§2)\n171\t    01-tuning.js           DH.TUNING defaults + difficulty tables (every dev slider reads/writes here, §4.21)\n172\t    05-glyphs.js           prompt badges (§4.15)\n173\t    10-art-*.js            drawables: art-train.js, art-cab.js, art-signals.js, art-station.js, art-town.js, art-landmarks.js, art-people.js, art-ui.js\n174\t    20-routes.js           route scripts: halo loop + depot (§5.1), zone scenery sets\n175\t    21-route-compiler.js   script → segments/objects/strips/things (§4.2)\n176\t    22-stages.js           stage definitions S0–S5 + PR (§5.3), story lines, postcards\n177\t    30-train.js            dynamics + lever (§4.3)\n178\t    31-signals.js          blocks, signals, ATS, other trains (§4.4)\n179\t    32-stations.js         approach, stop judgment, dwell/departure (§4.6)\n180\t    33-rules.js            speed limits, calls, horn, Halo Time, score, comfort (§4.5, 4.7, 4.9, 4.10)\n181\t    34-events.js           crossings, workers, obstruction, door rush, rival, oncoming, fog, glare, tips (§4.11)\n182\t    35-autopilot.js        AI driver (§4.19)\n183\t    40-sound.js            continuous soundscape + sfx + melodies + music (§4.16)\n184\t    41-babble.js           gibberish voices (§4.17)\n185\t    50-cab.js, 51-hud.js   cab overlay, HUD, stop gauge, stop cam (§4.14)\n186\t    52-story.js            briefings, radio chatter, subtitles, tips (§4.18)\n187\t    55-ui-*.js             title, menus, halo map, free run, briefing, results, game over, ending, log, help, about (§4.26)\n188\t    60-drive.js            the drive scene (§3.5)\n189\t    61-attract.js          attract mode + camera director (§4.20, §4.13)\n190\t    62-dev.js              dev mode + debug overlay (§4.21)\n191\t    63-hub.js              AI Hub session flow + card + ghosts (§4.23)\n192\t    64-duel.js             local split-screen duel (§4.24)\n193\t    99-start.js            boot steps, game.start, deep links (#gallery, #stage=S3, #attract, #dev ...)\n194\t  index.html               dev page: session.js first, then engine, rail.js, src/*.js (works from file://)\n195\t  test/run.mjs             THE one test command (§8)\n196\t  test/lib.mjs, test/*.test.mjs, test/browser.mjs, test/hub-harness.mjs\n197\t  tools/bundle.mjs         builds ../DenshaDeHalo-DenshaDeGo-<model>-<ts>.html (§9)\n198\t  tools/calibrate.mjs      runs the autopilot headless over every stage and prints par times (§4.8)\n199\t  ENGINE-CHANGES.md        every engine edit, one line of why each (feeds Engine Feedback)\n200\t  shots/                   screenshots for look review (§8.5)\n201\t```\n202\t\n203\t**Namespace rule.** Every src file starts with `(() => { 'use strict'; const E = My3D2dge, DH = (window.DH = window.DH || {}); ... })();`.\n204\tThe only globals are `My3D2dge`, `AIHub` and `DH`. `tools/bundle.mjs` concatenates the files in the same order as `index.html`.\n205\t\n206\t### 3.3 Scenes and flow\n207\t\n208\t```\n209\tboot (engine boot steps) ──► AIHub.active? ──yes──► hubCard ─► hubRun ─► hubEnd (stays; the hub removes the game)\n210\t                               │no\n211\t                               ▼\n212\t        ┌──────────────► title ◄──── any input ──── attract (10 s idle on title or any menu screen)\n213\t        │                 │\n214\t        │   ┌─────────────┼───────────────┬──────────────┬─────────────┬───────────┐\n215\t        │   ▼             ▼               ▼              ▼             ▼           ▼\n216\t        │ haloMap      freeRun         duelLobby      driversLog     help        about\n217\t        │ (career)     (setup)            │\n218\t        │   ▼             │               ▼\n219\t        │ briefing ───────┴──► drive ──► results ──► next briefing | haloMap      duel ─► duelResults\n220\t        │                       │  ▲         └─(S5)─► ending (credits) ─► title\n221\t        │                       │  └── pause (Shell): Resume · Retry stage · Retry from last station · Dev Mode · Settings · Controls · How to Drive · Quit\n222\t        │                       └──► gameOver ──► retry | continue from last station | haloMap\n223\t        └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n224\t```\n225\t\n226\t- `drive` is the only `pausable` gameplay scene; `duel` and `hubRun` are pausable too, each with a limited menu (§4.23).\n227\t- Use `game.go(name, data, { fade: 'wipe' })` for scene changes. Use `'iris'` into the Stop Cam and the ending.\n228\t- Deep links for testing: `#gallery`, `#stage=S2&s=5400&clock=10:17:30`, `#attract`, `#halomap`, `#results=S1`, `#duel`, `#about`.\n229\t\n230\t### 3.4 Per-step order in `drive` (fixed 1/120 s steps)\n231\t\n232\t1. Input becomes lever and button commands (or the autopilot writes the same commands, §4.19).\n233\t2. Train dynamics (§4.3).\n234\t3. Other trains move; block occupancy updates; signal aspects update (§4.4).\n235\t4. ATS and speed checks (§4.4, §4.5).\n236\t5. Events, crossings and fog (§4.11).\n237\t6. Station logic: approach, stop, judgment, dwell, departure (§4.6).\n238\t7. Call and horn windows (§4.7).\n239\t8. Halo Time, score, comfort (§4.9, §4.10).\n240\t9. Story triggers and tips (§4.18), then sound parameters (§4.16).\n241\t10. Camera (§4.13), then HUD state (§4.14).\n242\t11. Network or duel sync (§4.23, §4.24).\n243\t\n244\t**Draw order** (all inside `r.overlay`, screen pixels):\n245\t1. `rail.draw` (sky, then the world far to near);\n246\t2. weather overlays;\n247\t3. the cab;\n248\t4. the HUD;\n249\t5. call brackets and the glove;\n250\t6. subtitles and dialog;\n251\t7. toasts and judgments;\n252\t8. the Stop Cam inset;\n253\t9. the debug overlay.\n254\t\n255\t`draw` only reads state; it never changes it.\n256\t\n257\t### 3.5 Units and coordinates\n258\t\n259\t- `s`: metres along a route from its origin. On the halo route, s = 0 is Akari Central's 6-car stop marker, and the loop wraps at 20,600 m.\n260\t- `x`: metres across; **+ is to the right** in the direction of travel. Our track is at x = 0. Trains keep left as in Japan, so the counter-clockwise\n261\t  track is at x = +3.8.\n262\t- `y`: metres up. A segment's track height is absolute.\n263\t- Speeds: m/s inside the code, km/h in the UI. Accelerations are in **km/h/s** in all tables (1 km/h/s = 0.2778 m/s²).\n264\t- A train's reference point is its **front**. Cars are 20 m long, so 6 cars = 120 m and 10 cars = 200 m. The cab camera sits 1.5 m behind the front,\n265\t  2.9 m above the rail.\n266\t- Clock: seconds since midnight (06:40:00 = 24000). Game time drives it (1 s = 1 s). It pauses with the game.\n267\t- Characters: **1 m ≈ 15 engine units** (a 26-unit hero ≈ 1.7 m). A rig drawn at k pixels per metre uses a View scaled by k/15 (§4.1).\n268\t\n269\t### 3.6 Determinism and randomness\n270\t\n271\t- All world building and cosmetic randomness uses `DH.rng(label)`:\n272\t  - in a hub session, `AIHub.rng(label)`;\n273\t  - otherwise `E.rng(hash(label + ':' + stageSeed))`.\n274\t- Never use `Math.random`, `Date.now` or `performance.now` in game logic.\n275\t- The engine's `rand` and particles use `Math.random`. That's fine for frame-to-frame cosmetics, but no game state may depend on it.\n276\t- The hub harness only checks that `AIHub.seeded` is true on every copy. We build every world from our own streams, so all copies match anyway.\n277\t- `DH.proof(stageId, seconds)` runs a scripted autopilot drive and returns an FNV hash of the state samples. The test runs it twice and expects\n278\t  the same hash.\n279\t\n280\t### 3.7 `game.debug` handle (tests, tools/check.mjs, tools/replay.mjs)\n281\t\n282\t`snapshot()` returns:\n283\t- `scene`, `stage`, `s`, `km`, `v` (km/h), `notch` ('B3'), `brakeEff`, `grace`, `score`, `clock` ('06:41:12');\n284\t- `nextStop` ({ id, dist }), `lastJudgment`, `signals` (the next 3: { id, dist, aspect }), `limit`;\n285\t- `events` (ids fired), `comfort`, `doors`, `pilot`, `ats` ({ ringing, confirmed }), `camera`;\n286\t- `attract` ({ active, vignette }), `hub` ({ active, phase, sent, progressCalls }), `players` (duel), `errors`.\n287\t\n288\tFunctions:\n289\t- `jump(stageId, { s, clock, v })`\n290\t- `auto(on, { skill, cheat })`\n291\t- `setTod(h)`, `setWeather(w)`\n292\t- `forceAspect(signalId, aspect)`, `trigger(eventId)`\n293\t- `finishStage(perfect)`, `setGrace(n)`\n294\t\n295\tAlso set `game.stateHash = () => [s, v, grace, score]`, which makes recorded sessions catch divergence (`?record=1`, `tools/replay.mjs`).\n296\t\n297\t### 3.8 Engine changes (keep minimal; log each in `ENGINE-CHANGES.md`)\n298\t\n299\t1. **`engine/modules/rail.js` (new)**: the rail renderer (§4.1). It is a fork of road.js, because road.js can't do multiple tracks, raised platforms,\n300\t   long side objects (trains, buildings), rear cameras or square-pixel projection on wide screens.\n301\t2. **Dialog voice hook**: let `talk.voice` be a function `(ch, index, text, talk)`, called for each revealed character, so Babble can speak\n302\t   syllables (§4.17). Today `voice` is only an sfx name, blipped every second letter (`Dialog.update`, around line 8956).\n303\t3. **Settings screen filter**:\n304\t   - `ui.show('settings', { groups: ['Dev'], title: 'Dev Mode · Balance' })` shows only those groups.\n305\t   - The standard Settings screen hides the `Dev` group (`Shell._settingsRows`).\n306\t   - This gives live, controller-navigable sliders for free (§4.21).\n307\t4. **Glyphs**:\n308\t   - Make the standard `glyphs` setting default to `'playstation'` instead of `'auto'`; TASK.md wants PlayStation glyphs unless the player picks Xbox.\n309\t   - Add the 5×7 font glyphs `✕ ○ □ △`, so any `input.label()` text on canvas renders. The font currently has `×` but not these.\n310\t5. **ChipAudio accessors**: `audio.bus('sfx' | 'music' | 'master')` and `audio.noiseBuffer()`. The continuous train sound and Babble then route\n311\t   through the player's volume, mute and duck settings.\n312\t6. **Humanoid poses**:\n313\t   - `'bow'`: torso pitched forward about 40°, hands at the thighs, head down.\n314\t   - `'point'`: right arm straight forward at shoulder height, index finger out.\n315\t   - `'flag'`: right arm raised; the game draws a small flag at `rig.hand()`.\n316\t   - Add them next to `cheer`/`wave` in `poseW` and the solver. Check with `tools/filmstrip.mjs`.\n317\t7. **Hub button rule**: while `AIHub.active` and Create (`Pad8`) is held, ignore Options (`Pad9`) as pause (hub README, Rules).\n318\t\n319\tAfter patching, rerun the handoff's own `node game/test.mjs` and `node kits/test.mjs road` to check nothing else broke.\n320\t\n321\t---\n322\t\n323\t## 4. Systems\n324\t\n325\tEach subsection ends with **Tests**. All tests run under `node test/run.mjs` (§8).\n326\t\n327\t### 4.1 Rail renderer (`DH.Rail`, module `rail.js`): the riskiest piece, so build it first\n328\t\n329\t**Model.** A route is a run of **5 m segments**. Each segment has:\n330\t- `i`, `s`;\n331\t- `curve`: the lateral bend added per segment, `= ±L²/R` m (+ bends right), eased over 20 m at each end;\n332\t- `y0`, `y1`;\n333\t- `zone`;\n334\t- `flags`: tunnel, bridge, crossing, viaduct, quad;\n335\t- `tracks`: `[{ id, x0, x1, electrified, kind }]`, with offsets at both segment ends so tracks can diverge;\n336\t- the lists of strips and things that touch it.\n337\t\n338\t**Camera.** `{ s, x, h, dir: 1 | -1, fov: 75, horizon: .40, lookX, lookY, pitchPx, rollPx, shake }`.\n339\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a6a22e8e-f9ad-4c1e-b19f-6f268b0ad619","uuid":"edb913bf-0917-46a8-b8a7-eb81b73deeb3","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:33:08.946Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174801__xc8e150/work/PLAN.md","content":"  - P2: ↑/↓ lever, `.` call, `/` horn, `,` ATS, L EB, `;` neutral, `'` view.\n  - Show these on the Duel lobby screen.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Architecture\n\n### 3.1 Stack and why\n\n- **my-3D2dge v0.85.2, full engine** (`my-3d2dge.js` from the handoff package). It includes every module, the HTML Shell (pause, settings, controls),\n  Menus, Dialog with portraits, Humanoid and Blob rigs, the chip synth, input with glyph labels and rumble, split screen, boot steps, store and\n  saves, and the headless `game.advance` / `game.debug` testing.\n  - Use the 2D engine only. The three.js 3D engine is not in the handoff package, it runs poorly headless, and its look isn't the engine's\n    native pixel style.\n- **New module `rail.js`**, our pseudo-3D railway renderer. It is a fork of `modules/road.js` (OutRun-style segments) extended for tracks, platforms,\n  trains and rear-facing cameras (§4.1). This is the heart of the game's look.\n- **AI Hub client `session.js` 1.4.0**, pasted unmodified as the first script in `<head>`, right after `<meta charset>`.\n- **No other libraries and no CDN.** The single HTML inlines everything, so it runs offline from `file://`.\n- **Tooling:** Node 18+; Playwright 1.63.0 (as pinned in the handoff `package.json`; reuse an installed Chromium if one is there); python3\n  `http.server` for the hub harness only.\n- **Resolution:** `res: 'ps1', expand: true` gives 320×240 as a minimum and about 427×240 on 16:9. Anchor all HUD to `r.W`/`r.H`.\n\n### 3.2 Dev folder layout\n\n```\nDenshaDeHalo-DenshaDeGo-<model>-<ts>/\n  engine/                  copy of dist/handoff (my-3d2dge.js patched per §3.8, tools/, docs/, package.json, kits/ for reference)\n  engine/modules/rail.js   NEW: the rail renderer (§4.1), loaded after my-3d2dge.js\n  vendor/aihub/            session.js (unmodified), harness.html, bridge.js, round.js (harness files are for tests only, never bundled)\n  src/                     the game, in load order (each file one IIFE writing only into the DH namespace):\n    00-core.js             DH namespace, E, the E.Game, constants, units, DH.rng, settings definitions, input map (§2)\n    01-tuning.js           DH.TUNING defaults + difficulty tables (every dev slider reads/writes here, §4.21)\n    05-glyphs.js           prompt badges (§4.15)\n    10-art-*.js            drawables: art-train.js, art-cab.js, art-signals.js, art-station.js, art-town.js, art-landmarks.js, art-people.js, art-ui.js\n    20-routes.js           route scripts: halo loop + depot (§5.1), zone scenery sets\n    21-route-compiler.js   script → segments/objects/strips/things (§4.2)\n    22-stages.js           stage definitions S0–S5 + PR (§5.3), story lines, postcards\n    30-train.js            dynamics + lever (§4.3)\n    31-signals.js          blocks, signals, ATS, other trains (§4.4)\n    32-stations.js         approach, stop judgment, dwell/departure (§4.6)\n    33-rules.js            speed limits, calls, horn, Halo Time, score, comfort (§4.5, 4.7, 4.9, 4.10)\n    34-events.js           crossings, workers, obstruction, door rush, rival, oncoming, fog, glare, tips (§4.11)\n    35-autopilot.js        AI driver (§4.19)\n    40-sound.js            continuous soundscape + sfx + melodies + music (§4.16)\n    41-babble.js           gibberish voices (§4.17)\n    50-cab.js, 51-hud.js   cab overlay, HUD, stop gauge, stop cam (§4.14)\n    52-story.js            briefings, radio chatter, subtitles, tips (§4.18)\n    55-ui-*.js             title, menus, halo map, free run, briefing, results, game over, ending, log, help, about (§4.26)\n    60-drive.js            the drive scene (§3.5)\n    61-attract.js          attract mode + camera director (§4.20, §4.13)\n    62-dev.js              dev mode + debug overlay (§4.21)\n    63-hub.js              AI Hub session flow + card + ghosts (§4.23)\n    64-duel.js             local split-screen duel (§4.24)\n    99-start.js            boot steps, game.start, deep links (#gallery, #stage=S3, #attract, #dev ...)\n  index.html               dev page: session.js first, then engine, rail.js, src/*.js (works from file://)\n  test/run.mjs             THE one test command (§8)\n  test/lib.mjs, test/*.test.mjs, test/browser.mjs, test/hub-harness.mjs\n  tools/bundle.mjs         builds ../DenshaDeHalo-DenshaDeGo-<model>-<ts>.html (§9)\n  tools/calibrate.mjs      runs the autopilot headless over every stage and prints par times (§4.8)\n  ENGINE-CHANGES.md        every engine edit, one line of why each (feeds Engine Feedback)\n  shots/                   screenshots for look review (§8.5)\n```\n\n**Namespace rule.** Every src file starts with `(() => { 'use strict'; const E = My3D2dge, DH = (window.DH = window.DH || {}); ... })();`.\nThe only globals are `My3D2dge`, `AIHub` and `DH`. `tools/bundle.mjs` concatenates the files in the same order as `index.html`.\n\n### 3.3 Scenes and flow\n\n```\nboot (engine boot steps) ──► AIHub.active? ──yes──► hubCard ─► hubRun ─► hubEnd (stays; the hub removes the game)\n                               │no\n                               ▼\n        ┌──────────────► title ◄──── any input ──── attract (10 s idle on title or any menu screen)\n        │                 │\n        │   ┌─────────────┼───────────────┬──────────────┬─────────────┬───────────┐\n        │   ▼             ▼               ▼              ▼             ▼           ▼\n        │ haloMap      freeRun         duelLobby      driversLog     help        about\n        │ (career)     (setup)            │\n        │   ▼             │               ▼\n        │ briefing ───────┴──► drive ──► results ──► next briefing | haloMap      duel ─► duelResults\n        │                       │  ▲         └─(S5)─► ending (credits) ─► title\n        │                       │  └── pause (Shell): Resume · Retry stage · Retry from last station · Dev Mode · Settings · Controls · How to Drive · Quit\n        │                       └──► gameOver ──► retry | continue from last station | haloMap\n        └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n```\n\n- `drive` is the only `pausable` gameplay scene; `duel` and `hubRun` are pausable too, each with a limited menu (§4.23).\n- Use `game.go(name, data, { fade: 'wipe' })` for scene changes. Use `'iris'` into the Stop Cam and the ending.\n- Deep links for testing: `#gallery`, `#stage=S2&s=5400&clock=10:17:30`, `#attract`, `#halomap`, `#results=S1`, `#duel`, `#about`.\n\n### 3.4 Per-step order in `drive` (fixed 1/120 s steps)\n\n1. Input becomes lever and button commands (or the autopilot writes the same commands, §4.19).\n2. Train dynamics (§4.3).\n3. Other trains move; block occupancy updates; signal aspects update (§4.4).\n4. ATS and speed checks (§4.4, §4.5).\n5. Events, crossings and fog (§4.11).\n6. Station logic: approach, stop, judgment, dwell, departure (§4.6).\n7. Call and horn windows (§4.7).\n8. Halo Time, score, comfort (§4.9, §4.10).\n9. Story triggers and tips (§4.18), then sound parameters (§4.16).\n10. Camera (§4.13), then HUD state (§4.14).\n11. Network or duel sync (§4.23, §4.24).\n\n**Draw order** (all inside `r.overlay`, screen pixels):\n1. `rail.draw` (sky, then the world far to near);\n2. weather overlays;\n3. the cab;\n4. the HUD;\n5. call brackets and the glove;\n6. subtitles and dialog;\n7. toasts and judgments;\n8. the Stop Cam inset;\n9. the debug overlay.\n\n`draw` only reads state; it never changes it.\n\n### 3.5 Units and coordinates\n\n- `s`: metres along a route from its origin. On the halo route, s = 0 is Akari Central's 6-car stop marker, and the loop wraps at 20,600 m.\n- `x`: metres across; **+ is to the right** in the direction of travel. Our track is at x = 0. Trains keep left as in Japan, so the counter-clockwise\n  track is at x = +3.8.\n- `y`: metres up. A segment's track height is absolute.\n- Speeds: m/s inside the code, km/h in the UI. Accelerations are in **km/h/s** in all tables (1 km/h/s = 0.2778 m/s²).\n- A train's reference point is its **front**. Cars are 20 m long, so 6 cars = 120 m and 10 cars = 200 m. The cab camera sits 1.5 m behind the front,\n  2.9 m above the rail.\n- Clock: seconds since midnight (06:40:00 = 24000). Game time drives it (1 s = 1 s). It pauses with the game.\n- Characters: **1 m ≈ 15 engine units** (a 26-unit hero ≈ 1.7 m). A rig drawn at k pixels per metre uses a View scaled by k/15 (§4.1).\n\n### 3.6 Determinism and randomness\n\n- All world building and cosmetic randomness uses `DH.rng(label)`:\n  - in a hub session, `AIHub.rng(label)`;\n  - otherwise `E.rng(hash(label + ':' + stageSeed))`.\n- Never use `Math.random`, `Date.now` or `performance.now` in game logic.\n- The engine's `rand` and particles use `Math.random`. That's fine for frame-to-frame cosmetics, but no game state may depend on it.\n- The hub harness only checks that `AIHub.seeded` is true on every copy. We build every world from our own streams, so all copies match anyway.\n- `DH.proof(stageId, seconds)` runs a scripted autopilot drive and returns an FNV hash of the state samples. The test runs it twice and expects\n  the same hash.\n\n### 3.7 `game.debug` handle (tests, tools/check.mjs, tools/replay.mjs)\n\n`snapshot()` returns:\n- `scene`, `stage`, `s`, `km`, `v` (km/h), `notch` ('B3'), `brakeEff`, `grace`, `score`, `clock` ('06:41:12');\n- `nextStop` ({ id, dist }), `lastJudgment`, `signals` (the next 3: { id, dist, aspect }), `limit`;\n- `events` (ids fired), `comfort`, `doors`, `pilot`, `ats` ({ ringing, confirmed }), `camera`;\n- `attract` ({ active, vignette }), `hub` ({ active, phase, sent, progressCalls }), `players` (duel), `errors`.\n\nFunctions:\n- `jump(stageId, { s, clock, v })`\n- `auto(on, { skill, cheat })`\n- `setTod(h)`, `setWeather(w)`\n- `forceAspect(signalId, aspect)`, `trigger(eventId)`\n- `finishStage(perfect)`, `setGrace(n)`\n\nAlso set `game.stateHash = () => [s, v, grace, score]`, which makes recorded sessions catch divergence (`?record=1`, `tools/replay.mjs`).\n\n### 3.8 Engine changes (keep minimal; log each in `ENGINE-CHANGES.md`)\n\n1. **`engine/modules/rail.js` (new)**: the rail renderer (§4.1). It is a fork of road.js, because road.js can't do multiple tracks, raised platforms,\n   long side objects (trains, buildings), rear cameras or square-pixel projection on wide screens.\n2. **Dialog voice hook**: let `talk.voice` be a function `(ch, index, text, talk)`, called for each revealed character, so Babble can speak\n   syllables (§4.17). Today `voice` is only an sfx name, blipped every second letter (`Dialog.update`, around line 8956).\n3. **Settings screen filter**:\n   - `ui.show('settings', { groups: ['Dev'], title: 'Dev Mode · Balance' })` shows only those groups.\n   - The standard Settings screen hides the `Dev` group (`Shell._settingsRows`).\n   - This gives live, controller-navigable sliders for free (§4.21).\n4. **Glyphs**:\n   - Make the standard `glyphs` setting default to `'playstation'` instead of `'auto'`; TASK.md wants PlayStation glyphs unless the player picks Xbox.\n   - Add the 5×7 font glyphs `✕ ○ □ △`, so any `input.label()` text on canvas renders. The font currently has `×` but not these.\n5. **ChipAudio accessors**: `audio.bus('sfx' | 'music' | 'master')` and `audio.noiseBuffer()`. The continuous train sound and Babble then route\n   through the player's volume, mute and duck settings.\n6. **Humanoid poses**:\n   - `'bow'`: torso pitched forward about 40°, hands at the thighs, head down.\n   - `'point'`: right arm straight forward at shoulder height, index finger out.\n   - `'flag'`: right arm raised; the game draws a small flag at `rig.hand()`.\n   - Add them next to `cheer`/`wave` in `poseW` and the solver. Check with `tools/filmstrip.mjs`.\n7. **Hub button rule**: while `AIHub.active` and Create (`Pad8`) is held, ignore Options (`Pad9`) as pause (hub README, Rules).\n\nAfter patching, rerun the handoff's own `node game/test.mjs` and `node kits/test.mjs road` to check nothing else broke.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Systems\n\nEach subsection ends with **Tests**. All tests run under `node test/run.mjs` (§8).\n\n### 4.1 Rail renderer (`DH.Rail`, module `rail.js`): the riskiest piece, so build it first\n\n**Model.** A route is a run of **5 m segments**. Each segment has:\n- `i`, `s`;\n- `curve`: the lateral bend added per segment, `= ±L²/R` m (+ bends right), eased over 20 m at each end;\n- `y0`, `y1`;\n- `zone`;\n- `flags`: tunnel, bridge, crossing, viaduct, quad;\n- `tracks`: `[{ id, x0, x1, electrified, kind }]`, with offsets at both segment ends so tracks can diverge;\n- the lists of strips and things that touch it.\n\n**Camera.** `{ s, x, h, dir: 1 | -1, fov: 75, horizon: .40, lookX, lookY, pitchPx, rollPx, shake }`.\n","numLines":200,"startLine":140,"totalLines":1943}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01FPCdGNLp3GWP3LMMKxAkPD","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
