{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgh2XYhwPezB6AevYz3tP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019DDqz94GDTL4NY6q2XcdjG","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174801__xc8e150/work/PLAN.md","offset":1296,"limit":200},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":15738,"cache_read_input_tokens":438823,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":15738},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a6a22e8e-f9ad-4c1e-b19f-6f268b0ad619","uuid":"66733692-a319-444d-9528-b3f958c98088","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:33:48.177Z","request_id":"req_011Cgh2XYUYBziDq54cJeZQM","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_019DDqz94GDTL4NY6q2XcdjG":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174801__xc8e150/work/PLAN.md","offset":1296,"limit":200}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019DDqz94GDTL4NY6q2XcdjG","type":"tool_result","content":"1296\t**Standard settings** (built in; don't rebuild them): volume, music, effects, reduce motion (turns off sway and flashes), screen filter (CRT/scanlines),\n1297\tcontrols rebinding, rumble, and so on.\n1298\t\n1299\tEverything stays readable with no colour vision: signal letters, judgment words and lamp positions.\n1300\t\n1301\t**Tests:** each setting applies (glyph family, lever flip, guide visible, auto calls, subtitles off hides the subtitle box); settings survive a reload via\n1302\t`E.store`.\n1303\t\n1304\t### 4.26 Front-end screens (`55-ui-*.js`): big, few items, pixel-art, controller-first\n1305\t\n1306\t- **Title:**\n1307\t  - The background is the rail renderer's platform camera at Akari Central at dawn, with a Halo 8000 gliding in.\n1308\t  - Logo: `E.font.title('DENSHA DE HALO!', ...)` (scale 4, gold gradient) with a glowing gold **halo ring** around the final \"O\", and Haro-kun\n1309\t    bouncing beside it.\n1310\t  - Subtitle: \"THE HALO LINE · AKARI CITY\".\n1311\t  - `E.Menu`: CAREER · FREE RUN · DUEL · DRIVER'S LOG · HOW TO DRIVE · SETTINGS · ABOUT & CREDITS. Hover moves the focus and click picks.\n1312\t  - A prompt line with the device glyph, and the version (`E.versionLabel()` plus the game version v1.0).\n1313\t  - Keep it clear of the top-right corner buttons.\n1314\t- **Halo Map** (stage select):\n1315\t  - A gold ring (radius about 0.32 × min(W, H)) with 12 station dots and labels.\n1316\t  - Each stage is an arc between its stations: glowing when selected, grey when locked, with its rank stamp when done. Haro-kun floats in the centre.\n1317\t  - The stage card on the right (below on tall screens): name, time, weather, train, stops, best.\n1318\t  - ←/→ or the stick go round the ring; hover an arc to select it; ✕ or a click to go; ○ back.\n1319\t- **Free Run setup:** a stage on the ring, plus 4 rows of ←/→ choices (Time, Weather, Train, Difficulty), then START.\n1320\t- **Briefing:** §4.18.\n1321\t- **Results:**\n1322\t  - the rank stamp slams in (a scale tween, a shake, the stamp sound);\n1323\t  - 5 big lines (Stops, Punctuality, Calls & Horn, Smoothness, Penalties) with a total;\n1324\t  - Halo Time left; Hoshino's line;\n1325\t  - any new postcard flip;\n1326\t  - buttons: NEXT STAGE / RETRY / HALO MAP.\n1327\t- **Game Over:** the cracked halo; Hoshino's line; RETRY STAGE / CONTINUE FROM LAST STATION (Halo Time set back to the start value, score halved) / HALO MAP.\n1328\t- **Ending** (after S5's results):\n1329\t  - the finale cinematic: platform cam; staff and crowd bow; Hoshino gives you his pocket watch (dialog);\n1330\t  - then credits rolling over a night chase cam circling the whole ring, to \"Evening Halo\";\n1331\t  - \"THANK YOU FOR RIDING THE HALO LINE\";\n1332\t  - then the title, with S5 marked done.\n1333\t- **How to Drive:** a Shell `help` screen with keys for the current device and 5 short sections: Lever, Stop on the mark, Be on time, Point and\n1334\t  call, Signals & ATS.\n1335\t- **About & Credits:** pixel pages, ↑/↓ to scroll and ←/→ for the page, mouse wheel to scroll:\n1336\t  1. Credits (an original homage to *Densha de Go!* (Taito), not affiliated; my-3D2dge by Michael Crosato, MIT; the AI Hub client; asset sets if\n1337\t     used: Kenney, KayKit, ambientCG CC0; made by the building model);\n1338\t  2. **Source Information** (every TASK.md field);\n1339\t  3. Testing Feedback;\n1340\t  4. Engine Feedback;\n1341\t  5. Prompt Feedback.\n1342\t  - The text lives in `src/55-ui-about.js` and is filled in at the end, the same as the chat reply and `exit-interview.json` (§9).\n1343\t\n1344\t**Tests:** each screen opens and closes with confirm and cancel; the halo map wraps; locked stages can't be started; mouse hover selects (`input.feed('move')`);\n1345\tAbout contains every Source Information label; results buttons route correctly.\n1346\t\n1347\t---\n1348\t\n1349\t## 5. Content\n1350\t\n1351\t### 5.1 Akari City and the Halo Line\n1352\t\n1353\tThe line runs clockwise as a loop of **20,600 m** with **12 stations**. It is double-track: ours at x 0, the counter-clockwise track at x +3.8.\n1354\tFrom 11,800 to 15,600 it is **quad-track**: tracks at −7, 0, +7, +14; island platforms span −5.4…−1.6 and +8.6…+12.4. Line colours: **Halo Gold**\n1355\t`#f2c230` and **Sky** `#3aa0e0`.\n1356\t\n1357\t| # | id | In-game name | Meaning | Stop (6-car s) | Platform | Zone | Landmark / character |\n1358\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n1359\t| 0 | akari | AKARI CENTRAL | Akari Central | 0 (≡ 20,600) | island + side, 240 m, big roof | downtown | terminal hall with clock tower; Station Master Ota |\n1360\t| 1 | hanabatake | HANABATAKE | Flower Fields | 1,600 | left, 170 m | suburb-flowers | greenhouses, flower rows; Kota the train-fan kid |\n1361\t| 2 | kujira | KUJIRA-BASHI | Whale Bridge | 3,450 | right, 170 m | riverside | whale-back steel arch over the river mouth (bridge 2,600–3,200) |\n1362\t| 3 | minato | MINATO-MAE | Harbor Front | 5,100 | left + freight yard right | harbor | gantry cranes, containers, ferry; seagulls |\n1363\t| 4 | todai | TODAI-SHITA | Below the Lighthouse | 6,950 | island with passing loop | cliff | lighthouse on the cliff; tunnel 6,050–6,550 |\n1364\t| 5 | okiku | OKIKU-DERA | Great Chrysanthemum Temple | 8,700 | left, wooden, 170 m | temple-town | five-storey pagoda, temple gate, festival; Grandma Fuji |\n1365\t| 6 | yuhi | YUHI-ZAKA | Sunset Slope | 10,450 | right, hilltop | hills | terraced houses, sea view, little shrine |\n1366\t| 7 | shotengai | SHOTENGAI | Shopping Arcade | 12,100 | 2 islands (quad), viaduct | city-elevated | arcade roofs, neon game centre; Kenji's office |\n1367\t| 8 | daigaku | DAIGAKU-MAE | University | 13,700 | 2 islands (quad) | campus | clock tower, ginkgo trees, bicycles |\n1368\t| 9 | koen | SAKURA-KOEN | Cherry Blossom Park | 15,300 | 2 islands (quad) | park | sakura, pond, the \"Akari Eye\" Ferris wheel; petals |\n1369\t| 10 | hoshimi | HOSHIMI-DAI | Stargazing Heights | 17,100 | left | hills-north | observatory dome |\n1370\t| 11 | kawasemi | KAWASEMI | Kingfisher | 18,800 | right | river-north | river bridge 19,200–19,500, fishermen, paddies |\n1371\t\n1372\t- **Stop markers and platform lengths:**\n1373\t  - Akari Central and the three quad-section stations (Shotengai, Daigaku-mae, Sakura-Koen) have both \"6\" and \"10\" markers, with the 10 placed\n1374\t    8 m past the 6. Their platforms are 220–245 m.\n1375\t  - Every other station has only a \"6\" marker, on a platform of about 180 m.\n1376\t- **The quad transition (11,650–11,800):** the counter-clockwise track swings out from +3.8 to +14 in a gentle S-curve, and tracks −7 and +7 branch\n1377\t  off. Do the same in reverse at 15,600–15,750. In normal service, 0 and +7 carry clockwise trains (the Halo local and the Sky Liner express), and\n1378\t  −7 and +14 carry counter-clockwise ones.\n1379\t- **Station kit** (things and strips): name boards every 40 m (white; big romaji; English meaning smaller; previous and next stations with\n1380\t  arrows), canopy and columns, benches, vending machines (red/blue/white with lit panels), sorting bins, a platform clock, LED departure board,\n1381\t  stair housings, a safety fence, door-queue marks, staff at the head end, a Haro-kun poster.\n1382\t- In-game text is ASCII (the font has no kana or macrons), so names have no macrons: TODAI-SHITA, OKIKU-DERA, SHOTENGAI.\n1383\t\n1384\t**Zones** (scenery sets; buildings come from a parametric box generator, §5.6):\n1385\t\n1386\t| zone | s range | ground | buildings (weights) | nature | props | backdrop |\n1387\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n1388\t| downtown | 19,900–700 | concrete | office towers .4, department store .2, hotels .2, overpasses | street trees | billboards (Haro-kun ads), lamp posts, vending machines | city skyline |\n1389\t| suburb-flowers | 700–2,500 | fields/grass | houses .5 (blue/grey/terracotta roofs), apartments with balconies and laundry .3, greenhouses .1, konbini .1 | flower rows, paddies | utility poles and wires, bikes, crossing mirrors | hills, far city |\n1390\t| riverside | 2,500–3,600 | water/reeds | boat sheds | reeds, willows | fishermen, rowboats (library) | river mouth, sea |\n1391\t| harbor | 3,600–5,800 | asphalt | warehouses (long strips with roll-up doors) .5, container stacks .4 | — | gantry cranes, crates/barrels (library), bollards, seagulls | sea, ships |\n1392\t| cliff | 5,800–7,500 | rock/grass | fishing houses | pines (library), rocks | stone walls, tunnel portals | sea, cliffs |\n1393\t| temple-town | 7,500–9,300 | gravel | machiya (dark wood, tiled roofs) .6, shops with noren .4 | pines, maples, stone lanterns | lantern strings, torii, stalls | hills, pagoda |\n1394\t| hills | 9,300–11,700 | slopes | terrace houses | cedars, bamboo | retaining walls, guard rails | sea (left), sunset |\n1395\t| city-elevated | 11,700–13,200 | rooftops below the viaduct | arcade roofs, neon facades, apartment towers | — | sound walls, billboards | skyline |\n1396\t| campus | 13,200–14,500 | lawns | university blocks, gym dome | ginkgo | bike rows, students | city |\n1397\t| park | 14,500–16,000 | grass | pavilion | sakura (petal particles) | lanterns, benches (library) | hills, Ferris wheel |\n1398\t| hills-north | 16,000–18,000 | grass/forest | houses | cedars | poles | mountains, stars |\n1399\t| river-north | 18,000–19,700 | paddies/water | farmhouses | reeds | scarecrows, fishermen | mountains |\n1400\t| depot | depot route | gravel | depot sheds (strips), pits | — | lamps, workers, parked trains | dawn city |\n1401\t\n1402\t**Depot route** (S0): 1,000 m on a single track with sidings at x ±4.5 holding parked trains (0–350); straight to 400, a curve R 800 L from 400 to 600,\n1403\tthen straight. Stop marks (yellow boards) at 300, 620 and 900. A staff halt platform \"DEPOT GATE\" on the left at 860–920. A shunting signal at 40.\n1404\t\n1405\t### 5.2 Trains\n1406\t\n1407\t| id | name | cab | notches | traction a0 (km/h/s) | brakes | lags (apply/release/power) | vmax | sound | livery |\n1408\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n1409\t| `h8000` | HALO 8000 | modern grey panel, one T-handle, LCD notch display | P5 / B8 | .8 1.4 2.0 2.6 3.2 (vk 15 25 35 40 45) | 0.5·n, EB 5.0 | .7 / .5 / .3 s | 110 | VVVF \"singing\" | silver, gold halo stripe, sky band |\n1410\t| `h3000` | HALO 3000 (retro) | green panel, two handles, analog gauges | P4 / B7 | .7 1.3 1.9 2.5 (vk 18 28 36 42) | 0.55·n, EB 4.6 | 1.1 / .8 / .5 s | 100 | resistor growl and clunks | cream, orange stripe |\n1411\t| `skyliner` | SKY LINER (rival) | — | AI | — | — | — | 120 | — | purple and silver |\n1412\t| `freight` | MINATO FREIGHT | — | AI | — | — | — | 75 | — | blue loco plus colourful containers |\n1413\t| `inner` | HALO 8000 inner loop | — | AI | — | — | — | — | — | as h8000 |\n1414\t\n1415\t- Formations: `h8000-6`, `h8000-10` (S4), `h3000-6` (S2).\n1416\t\n1417\t### 5.3 Stages\n1418\t\n1419\tTimes are initial values; calibrate them (§4.8). \"s\" means route metres.\n1420\t\n1421\t**S0 · DAWN DEPOT** (tutorial). 05:30 dawn, clear, `h8000-6`, depot route, Halo Time frozen.\n1422\t\n1423\tSteps, each a Hoshino line with a prompt; the next unlocks when the condition holds:\n1424\t1. P1, reach 10 km/h.\n1425\t2. N, coast.\n1426\t3. Brake: get below 5 km/h.\n1427\t4. Stop at Mark 1 (300); judged with no penalty; Stop Cam explained.\n1428\t5. The departure call on the shunting signal.\n1429\t6. Up to 40 under the \"40\" board.\n1430\t7. Mark 2 (620), easing to B1: SMOOTH explained.\n1431\t8. EB demo (pull, stop, release).\n1432\t9. Mark 3 (900) within 1 m to pass; retry the step on failure.\n1433\t\n1434\tThe certificate stamp follows, then S1 unlocks. Halo Time, ATS and the horn get one sentence each from Hoshino (\"You'll meet those in service\").\n1435\t\n1436\t**S1 · FIRST LIGHT LOCAL.** 06:40 dawn into morning, clear, `h8000-6`, Akari Central → Hanabatake → Kujira-bashi.\n1437\t\n1438\t| stop | arr | dep |\n1439\t|---|---|---|\n1440\t| AKARI CENTRAL | — | 06:40:00 |\n1441\t| HANABATAKE | 06:42:05 | 06:42:30 |\n1442\t| KUJIRA-BASHI | 06:44:45 | — |\n1443\t\n1444\tGeometry (route script excerpt, the pattern for every stage):\n1445\t```\n1446\t[-230,'station',{id:'akari',side:'island',len:245,stop:{6:0,10:8},roof:[-215,5],melody:'akari',crowd:3,landmark:'terminal'}]\n1447\t[0,'zone','downtown'] [60,'signal',{id:'AK-S',kind:'start'}] [150,'overpass',{w:18,h:7}]\n1448\t[200,'limit',{v:45,until:420}] [420,'limit',{v:85}] [520,'curve',{len:260,r:900,dir:'R'}]\n1449\t[700,'zone','suburb-flowers'] [700,'signal',{id:'B101',kind:'block'}]\n1450\t[880,'limit',{v:70,until:1260}] [900,'curve',{len:330,r:500,dir:'L'}]\n1451\t[1050,'horn',{}] [1110,'crossing',{id:'X1',road:6,cars:3,peds:2}] [1250,'signal',{id:'B102',kind:'block'}]\n1452\t[1380,'signal',{id:'HB-H',kind:'home'}] [1420,'station',{id:'hanabatake',side:'L',len:190,stop:{6:1600},melody:'hanabatake',crowd:2}]\n1453\t[1660,'signal',{id:'HB-S',kind:'start'}] [1800,'grade',{len:300,permille:8}] [2150,'signal',{id:'B103',kind:'block'}]\n1454\t[2300,'horn',{}] [2450,'limit',{v:75,until:3250}] [2500,'zone','riverside'] [2600,'bridge',{len:600,kind:'truss',water:'river'}]\n1455\t[2700,'curve',{len:400,r:1200,dir:'R'}] [2950,'signal',{id:'B104',kind:'block'}] [3250,'signal',{id:'KJ-H',kind:'home'}]\n1456\t[3290,'station',{id:'kujira',side:'R',len:175,stop:{6:3450},melody:'kujira',crowd:2}]\n1457\t```\n1458\t\n1459\t- Events: crossing X1 (normal); `oncoming` at 2,000; Kota waves at Hanabatake (dwell); radio lines (§5.5).\n1460\t- Teaches: the timetable and clock, the departure procedure, calls, the horn board, a limit board, an oncoming train, crossing bells, melodies and\n1461\t  announcements.\n1462\t\n1463\t**S2 · HARBOR RAIN RAPID.** 10:15 day, **rain**, `h3000-6`, Kujira-bashi → Minato-mae → (pass Todai-shita) → Okiku-dera.\n1464\t\n1465\t| stop | arr | dep |\n1466\t|---|---|---|\n1467\t| KUJIRA-BASHI | — | 10:15:00 |\n1468\t| MINATO-MAE | 10:16:55 | 10:17:20 |\n1469\t| TODAI-SHITA | pass 10:19:50 | |\n1470\t| OKIKU-DERA | 10:22:00 | — |\n1471\t\n1472\t- Geometry: line speed 95 (Rapid); curve R 700 L at 3,700–4,000 (limit 80).\n1473\t  - Signals: B201 3,900, B202 4,300, MN-H 4,880 (the Minato-mae platform runs 4,925–5,115), MN-S 5,160, **M5600** 5,600, **M6000** 6,000,\n1474\t    B205 6,600, TD-H 6,850 (main line through, no platform stop), B207 7,600, OK-H 8,480 (the Okiku-dera platform runs 8,530–8,715).\n1475\t  - Tunnel 6,050–6,550 with a curve R 400 R (limit 60, horn board 5,950).\n1476\t  - Pass board at 6,550. Freight loop at Todai-shita on the left, 6,750–7,150.\n1477\t- **Freight script** (260 m long):\n1478\t  - It joins our track from the Minato yard at 5,250 at **10:16:20** and runs at 45 km/h (12.5 m/s).\n1479\t  - It **stops with its front at 6,300 from about 10:17:44 for 40 s** (points being set), then pulls on and diverges into the Todai loop at 6,780,\n1480\t    where it stands.\n1481\t  - What the player gets, at par:\n1482\t    - At our 10:17:20 departure its rear is in block M5600–M6000, so the starting signal MN-S shows **Y** (call: \"Chui!\").\n1483\t    - Near 10:17:56 we pass M6000's ATS beacon at 5,400. M6000 is **R** (the freight is standing in block 6,000–6,600), so the **ATS bell rings**.\n1484\t    - We stop before M6000 at about 10:18:56. Its rear clears 6,600 at about 10:19:14, so M6000 turns **Y** after a wait of about 20 s, then\n1485\t      **G** once the freight is in the loop (about 10:19:45).\n1486\t  - We see its tail lights through the rain while we arrive at Minato-mae, and later pass it standing in the loop at Todai-shita.\n1487\t  - The test (§4.4) checks this sequence with the autopilot.\n1488\t- Teaches: another train type (two handles, slow brakes), rain slip and slide, yellow signals, ATS confirm, a tunnel, a pass station.\n1489\t\n1490\t**S3 · TEMPLE HILL LOCAL.** 14:00 afternoon haze, clear, `h8000-6`, Okiku-dera → Yuhi-zaka → Shotengai. The stage **opens during the festival dwell**\n1491\tat Okiku-dera.\n1492\t\n1493\t| stop | arr | dep |\n1494\t|---|---|---|\n1495\t| OKIKU-DERA | (dwell) | 14:00:00 |"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a6a22e8e-f9ad-4c1e-b19f-6f268b0ad619","uuid":"c2258342-8fb9-4c70-ab58-6565014f0f25","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:33:48.184Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174801__xc8e150/work/PLAN.md","content":"**Standard settings** (built in; don't rebuild them): volume, music, effects, reduce motion (turns off sway and flashes), screen filter (CRT/scanlines),\ncontrols rebinding, rumble, and so on.\n\nEverything stays readable with no colour vision: signal letters, judgment words and lamp positions.\n\n**Tests:** each setting applies (glyph family, lever flip, guide visible, auto calls, subtitles off hides the subtitle box); settings survive a reload via\n`E.store`.\n\n### 4.26 Front-end screens (`55-ui-*.js`): big, few items, pixel-art, controller-first\n\n- **Title:**\n  - The background is the rail renderer's platform camera at Akari Central at dawn, with a Halo 8000 gliding in.\n  - Logo: `E.font.title('DENSHA DE HALO!', ...)` (scale 4, gold gradient) with a glowing gold **halo ring** around the final \"O\", and Haro-kun\n    bouncing beside it.\n  - Subtitle: \"THE HALO LINE · AKARI CITY\".\n  - `E.Menu`: CAREER · FREE RUN · DUEL · DRIVER'S LOG · HOW TO DRIVE · SETTINGS · ABOUT & CREDITS. Hover moves the focus and click picks.\n  - A prompt line with the device glyph, and the version (`E.versionLabel()` plus the game version v1.0).\n  - Keep it clear of the top-right corner buttons.\n- **Halo Map** (stage select):\n  - A gold ring (radius about 0.32 × min(W, H)) with 12 station dots and labels.\n  - Each stage is an arc between its stations: glowing when selected, grey when locked, with its rank stamp when done. Haro-kun floats in the centre.\n  - The stage card on the right (below on tall screens): name, time, weather, train, stops, best.\n  - ←/→ or the stick go round the ring; hover an arc to select it; ✕ or a click to go; ○ back.\n- **Free Run setup:** a stage on the ring, plus 4 rows of ←/→ choices (Time, Weather, Train, Difficulty), then START.\n- **Briefing:** §4.18.\n- **Results:**\n  - the rank stamp slams in (a scale tween, a shake, the stamp sound);\n  - 5 big lines (Stops, Punctuality, Calls & Horn, Smoothness, Penalties) with a total;\n  - Halo Time left; Hoshino's line;\n  - any new postcard flip;\n  - buttons: NEXT STAGE / RETRY / HALO MAP.\n- **Game Over:** the cracked halo; Hoshino's line; RETRY STAGE / CONTINUE FROM LAST STATION (Halo Time set back to the start value, score halved) / HALO MAP.\n- **Ending** (after S5's results):\n  - the finale cinematic: platform cam; staff and crowd bow; Hoshino gives you his pocket watch (dialog);\n  - then credits rolling over a night chase cam circling the whole ring, to \"Evening Halo\";\n  - \"THANK YOU FOR RIDING THE HALO LINE\";\n  - then the title, with S5 marked done.\n- **How to Drive:** a Shell `help` screen with keys for the current device and 5 short sections: Lever, Stop on the mark, Be on time, Point and\n  call, Signals & ATS.\n- **About & Credits:** pixel pages, ↑/↓ to scroll and ←/→ for the page, mouse wheel to scroll:\n  1. Credits (an original homage to *Densha de Go!* (Taito), not affiliated; my-3D2dge by Michael Crosato, MIT; the AI Hub client; asset sets if\n     used: Kenney, KayKit, ambientCG CC0; made by the building model);\n  2. **Source Information** (every TASK.md field);\n  3. Testing Feedback;\n  4. Engine Feedback;\n  5. Prompt Feedback.\n  - The text lives in `src/55-ui-about.js` and is filled in at the end, the same as the chat reply and `exit-interview.json` (§9).\n\n**Tests:** each screen opens and closes with confirm and cancel; the halo map wraps; locked stages can't be started; mouse hover selects (`input.feed('move')`);\nAbout contains every Source Information label; results buttons route correctly.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Content\n\n### 5.1 Akari City and the Halo Line\n\nThe line runs clockwise as a loop of **20,600 m** with **12 stations**. It is double-track: ours at x 0, the counter-clockwise track at x +3.8.\nFrom 11,800 to 15,600 it is **quad-track**: tracks at −7, 0, +7, +14; island platforms span −5.4…−1.6 and +8.6…+12.4. Line colours: **Halo Gold**\n`#f2c230` and **Sky** `#3aa0e0`.\n\n| # | id | In-game name | Meaning | Stop (6-car s) | Platform | Zone | Landmark / character |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 0 | akari | AKARI CENTRAL | Akari Central | 0 (≡ 20,600) | island + side, 240 m, big roof | downtown | terminal hall with clock tower; Station Master Ota |\n| 1 | hanabatake | HANABATAKE | Flower Fields | 1,600 | left, 170 m | suburb-flowers | greenhouses, flower rows; Kota the train-fan kid |\n| 2 | kujira | KUJIRA-BASHI | Whale Bridge | 3,450 | right, 170 m | riverside | whale-back steel arch over the river mouth (bridge 2,600–3,200) |\n| 3 | minato | MINATO-MAE | Harbor Front | 5,100 | left + freight yard right | harbor | gantry cranes, containers, ferry; seagulls |\n| 4 | todai | TODAI-SHITA | Below the Lighthouse | 6,950 | island with passing loop | cliff | lighthouse on the cliff; tunnel 6,050–6,550 |\n| 5 | okiku | OKIKU-DERA | Great Chrysanthemum Temple | 8,700 | left, wooden, 170 m | temple-town | five-storey pagoda, temple gate, festival; Grandma Fuji |\n| 6 | yuhi | YUHI-ZAKA | Sunset Slope | 10,450 | right, hilltop | hills | terraced houses, sea view, little shrine |\n| 7 | shotengai | SHOTENGAI | Shopping Arcade | 12,100 | 2 islands (quad), viaduct | city-elevated | arcade roofs, neon game centre; Kenji's office |\n| 8 | daigaku | DAIGAKU-MAE | University | 13,700 | 2 islands (quad) | campus | clock tower, ginkgo trees, bicycles |\n| 9 | koen | SAKURA-KOEN | Cherry Blossom Park | 15,300 | 2 islands (quad) | park | sakura, pond, the \"Akari Eye\" Ferris wheel; petals |\n| 10 | hoshimi | HOSHIMI-DAI | Stargazing Heights | 17,100 | left | hills-north | observatory dome |\n| 11 | kawasemi | KAWASEMI | Kingfisher | 18,800 | right | river-north | river bridge 19,200–19,500, fishermen, paddies |\n\n- **Stop markers and platform lengths:**\n  - Akari Central and the three quad-section stations (Shotengai, Daigaku-mae, Sakura-Koen) have both \"6\" and \"10\" markers, with the 10 placed\n    8 m past the 6. Their platforms are 220–245 m.\n  - Every other station has only a \"6\" marker, on a platform of about 180 m.\n- **The quad transition (11,650–11,800):** the counter-clockwise track swings out from +3.8 to +14 in a gentle S-curve, and tracks −7 and +7 branch\n  off. Do the same in reverse at 15,600–15,750. In normal service, 0 and +7 carry clockwise trains (the Halo local and the Sky Liner express), and\n  −7 and +14 carry counter-clockwise ones.\n- **Station kit** (things and strips): name boards every 40 m (white; big romaji; English meaning smaller; previous and next stations with\n  arrows), canopy and columns, benches, vending machines (red/blue/white with lit panels), sorting bins, a platform clock, LED departure board,\n  stair housings, a safety fence, door-queue marks, staff at the head end, a Haro-kun poster.\n- In-game text is ASCII (the font has no kana or macrons), so names have no macrons: TODAI-SHITA, OKIKU-DERA, SHOTENGAI.\n\n**Zones** (scenery sets; buildings come from a parametric box generator, §5.6):\n\n| zone | s range | ground | buildings (weights) | nature | props | backdrop |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| downtown | 19,900–700 | concrete | office towers .4, department store .2, hotels .2, overpasses | street trees | billboards (Haro-kun ads), lamp posts, vending machines | city skyline |\n| suburb-flowers | 700–2,500 | fields/grass | houses .5 (blue/grey/terracotta roofs), apartments with balconies and laundry .3, greenhouses .1, konbini .1 | flower rows, paddies | utility poles and wires, bikes, crossing mirrors | hills, far city |\n| riverside | 2,500–3,600 | water/reeds | boat sheds | reeds, willows | fishermen, rowboats (library) | river mouth, sea |\n| harbor | 3,600–5,800 | asphalt | warehouses (long strips with roll-up doors) .5, container stacks .4 | — | gantry cranes, crates/barrels (library), bollards, seagulls | sea, ships |\n| cliff | 5,800–7,500 | rock/grass | fishing houses | pines (library), rocks | stone walls, tunnel portals | sea, cliffs |\n| temple-town | 7,500–9,300 | gravel | machiya (dark wood, tiled roofs) .6, shops with noren .4 | pines, maples, stone lanterns | lantern strings, torii, stalls | hills, pagoda |\n| hills | 9,300–11,700 | slopes | terrace houses | cedars, bamboo | retaining walls, guard rails | sea (left), sunset |\n| city-elevated | 11,700–13,200 | rooftops below the viaduct | arcade roofs, neon facades, apartment towers | — | sound walls, billboards | skyline |\n| campus | 13,200–14,500 | lawns | university blocks, gym dome | ginkgo | bike rows, students | city |\n| park | 14,500–16,000 | grass | pavilion | sakura (petal particles) | lanterns, benches (library) | hills, Ferris wheel |\n| hills-north | 16,000–18,000 | grass/forest | houses | cedars | poles | mountains, stars |\n| river-north | 18,000–19,700 | paddies/water | farmhouses | reeds | scarecrows, fishermen | mountains |\n| depot | depot route | gravel | depot sheds (strips), pits | — | lamps, workers, parked trains | dawn city |\n\n**Depot route** (S0): 1,000 m on a single track with sidings at x ±4.5 holding parked trains (0–350); straight to 400, a curve R 800 L from 400 to 600,\nthen straight. Stop marks (yellow boards) at 300, 620 and 900. A staff halt platform \"DEPOT GATE\" on the left at 860–920. A shunting signal at 40.\n\n### 5.2 Trains\n\n| id | name | cab | notches | traction a0 (km/h/s) | brakes | lags (apply/release/power) | vmax | sound | livery |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `h8000` | HALO 8000 | modern grey panel, one T-handle, LCD notch display | P5 / B8 | .8 1.4 2.0 2.6 3.2 (vk 15 25 35 40 45) | 0.5·n, EB 5.0 | .7 / .5 / .3 s | 110 | VVVF \"singing\" | silver, gold halo stripe, sky band |\n| `h3000` | HALO 3000 (retro) | green panel, two handles, analog gauges | P4 / B7 | .7 1.3 1.9 2.5 (vk 18 28 36 42) | 0.55·n, EB 4.6 | 1.1 / .8 / .5 s | 100 | resistor growl and clunks | cream, orange stripe |\n| `skyliner` | SKY LINER (rival) | — | AI | — | — | — | 120 | — | purple and silver |\n| `freight` | MINATO FREIGHT | — | AI | — | — | — | 75 | — | blue loco plus colourful containers |\n| `inner` | HALO 8000 inner loop | — | AI | — | — | — | — | — | as h8000 |\n\n- Formations: `h8000-6`, `h8000-10` (S4), `h3000-6` (S2).\n\n### 5.3 Stages\n\nTimes are initial values; calibrate them (§4.8). \"s\" means route metres.\n\n**S0 · DAWN DEPOT** (tutorial). 05:30 dawn, clear, `h8000-6`, depot route, Halo Time frozen.\n\nSteps, each a Hoshino line with a prompt; the next unlocks when the condition holds:\n1. P1, reach 10 km/h.\n2. N, coast.\n3. Brake: get below 5 km/h.\n4. Stop at Mark 1 (300); judged with no penalty; Stop Cam explained.\n5. The departure call on the shunting signal.\n6. Up to 40 under the \"40\" board.\n7. Mark 2 (620), easing to B1: SMOOTH explained.\n8. EB demo (pull, stop, release).\n9. Mark 3 (900) within 1 m to pass; retry the step on failure.\n\nThe certificate stamp follows, then S1 unlocks. Halo Time, ATS and the horn get one sentence each from Hoshino (\"You'll meet those in service\").\n\n**S1 · FIRST LIGHT LOCAL.** 06:40 dawn into morning, clear, `h8000-6`, Akari Central → Hanabatake → Kujira-bashi.\n\n| stop | arr | dep |\n|---|---|---|\n| AKARI CENTRAL | — | 06:40:00 |\n| HANABATAKE | 06:42:05 | 06:42:30 |\n| KUJIRA-BASHI | 06:44:45 | — |\n\nGeometry (route script excerpt, the pattern for every stage):\n```\n[-230,'station',{id:'akari',side:'island',len:245,stop:{6:0,10:8},roof:[-215,5],melody:'akari',crowd:3,landmark:'terminal'}]\n[0,'zone','downtown'] [60,'signal',{id:'AK-S',kind:'start'}] [150,'overpass',{w:18,h:7}]\n[200,'limit',{v:45,until:420}] [420,'limit',{v:85}] [520,'curve',{len:260,r:900,dir:'R'}]\n[700,'zone','suburb-flowers'] [700,'signal',{id:'B101',kind:'block'}]\n[880,'limit',{v:70,until:1260}] [900,'curve',{len:330,r:500,dir:'L'}]\n[1050,'horn',{}] [1110,'crossing',{id:'X1',road:6,cars:3,peds:2}] [1250,'signal',{id:'B102',kind:'block'}]\n[1380,'signal',{id:'HB-H',kind:'home'}] [1420,'station',{id:'hanabatake',side:'L',len:190,stop:{6:1600},melody:'hanabatake',crowd:2}]\n[1660,'signal',{id:'HB-S',kind:'start'}] [1800,'grade',{len:300,permille:8}] [2150,'signal',{id:'B103',kind:'block'}]\n[2300,'horn',{}] [2450,'limit',{v:75,until:3250}] [2500,'zone','riverside'] [2600,'bridge',{len:600,kind:'truss',water:'river'}]\n[2700,'curve',{len:400,r:1200,dir:'R'}] [2950,'signal',{id:'B104',kind:'block'}] [3250,'signal',{id:'KJ-H',kind:'home'}]\n[3290,'station',{id:'kujira',side:'R',len:175,stop:{6:3450},melody:'kujira',crowd:2}]\n```\n\n- Events: crossing X1 (normal); `oncoming` at 2,000; Kota waves at Hanabatake (dwell); radio lines (§5.5).\n- Teaches: the timetable and clock, the departure procedure, calls, the horn board, a limit board, an oncoming train, crossing bells, melodies and\n  announcements.\n\n**S2 · HARBOR RAIN RAPID.** 10:15 day, **rain**, `h3000-6`, Kujira-bashi → Minato-mae → (pass Todai-shita) → Okiku-dera.\n\n| stop | arr | dep |\n|---|---|---|\n| KUJIRA-BASHI | — | 10:15:00 |\n| MINATO-MAE | 10:16:55 | 10:17:20 |\n| TODAI-SHITA | pass 10:19:50 | |\n| OKIKU-DERA | 10:22:00 | — |\n\n- Geometry: line speed 95 (Rapid); curve R 700 L at 3,700–4,000 (limit 80).\n  - Signals: B201 3,900, B202 4,300, MN-H 4,880 (the Minato-mae platform runs 4,925–5,115), MN-S 5,160, **M5600** 5,600, **M6000** 6,000,\n    B205 6,600, TD-H 6,850 (main line through, no platform stop), B207 7,600, OK-H 8,480 (the Okiku-dera platform runs 8,530–8,715).\n  - Tunnel 6,050–6,550 with a curve R 400 R (limit 60, horn board 5,950).\n  - Pass board at 6,550. Freight loop at Todai-shita on the left, 6,750–7,150.\n- **Freight script** (260 m long):\n  - It joins our track from the Minato yard at 5,250 at **10:16:20** and runs at 45 km/h (12.5 m/s).\n  - It **stops with its front at 6,300 from about 10:17:44 for 40 s** (points being set), then pulls on and diverges into the Todai loop at 6,780,\n    where it stands.\n  - What the player gets, at par:\n    - At our 10:17:20 departure its rear is in block M5600–M6000, so the starting signal MN-S shows **Y** (call: \"Chui!\").\n    - Near 10:17:56 we pass M6000's ATS beacon at 5,400. M6000 is **R** (the freight is standing in block 6,000–6,600), so the **ATS bell rings**.\n    - We stop before M6000 at about 10:18:56. Its rear clears 6,600 at about 10:19:14, so M6000 turns **Y** after a wait of about 20 s, then\n      **G** once the freight is in the loop (about 10:19:45).\n  - We see its tail lights through the rain while we arrive at Minato-mae, and later pass it standing in the loop at Todai-shita.\n  - The test (§4.4) checks this sequence with the autopilot.\n- Teaches: another train type (two handles, slow brakes), rain slip and slide, yellow signals, ATS confirm, a tunnel, a pass station.\n\n**S3 · TEMPLE HILL LOCAL.** 14:00 afternoon haze, clear, `h8000-6`, Okiku-dera → Yuhi-zaka → Shotengai. The stage **opens during the festival dwell**\nat Okiku-dera.\n\n| stop | arr | dep |\n|---|---|---|\n| OKIKU-DERA | (dwell) | 14:00:00 |","numLines":200,"startLine":1296,"totalLines":1945}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_019DDqz94GDTL4NY6q2XcdjG","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
