{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01YJHEyKbQyZmFZbJGHkV3gN","type":"tool_result","content":"1495\t| OKIKU-DERA | (dwell) | 14:00:00 |\n1496\t| YUHI-ZAKA | 14:02:40 | 14:03:00 |\n1497\t| SHOTENGAI | 14:05:30 | — |\n1498\t\n1499\t- Geometry:\n1500\t  - crossing X2 at 9,050 (normal);\n1501\t  - climb **25‰** from 9,200 to 10,300; curve R 600 R at 9,300–9,600; curve R 450 L at 9,900–10,200 (limit 60);\n1502\t  - horn board 9,450; **workers** with a slow order of 25 from 9,600 to 9,900 (lookout at 9,550);\n1503\t  - Yuhi-zaka at 10,450;\n1504\t  - descent **20‰** from 10,700 to 11,450; curve R 500 L at 10,900–11,200 (limit 55);\n1505\t  - **obstruction emitter at 11,150 for crossing X3 at 11,500** (the festival's takoyaki cart); horn board 11,400;\n1506\t  - viaduct from 11,700; Shotengai at 12,100.\n1507\t- Events: festival (crowd ×2, lanterns, taiko), `workers`, `obstruction` at X3 (clears 12 s after we stop), Grandma Fuji bows at Yuhi-zaka, `oncoming`\n1508\t  at 11,200.\n1509\t- Teaches: gradients both ways, a slow order and the horn for workers, an emergency stop, a festival crowd.\n1510\t\n1511\t**S4 · SUNSET RUSH.** 17:30 sunset, clear, **`h8000-10`** (10-car marker), Shotengai → Daigaku-mae → Sakura-Koen, quad track.\n1512\t\n1513\t| stop | arr | dep |\n1514\t|---|---|---|\n1515\t| SHOTENGAI | — | 17:30:00 |\n1516\t| DAIGAKU-MAE | 17:31:55 | 17:32:15 |\n1517\t| SAKURA-KOEN | 17:34:05 | — |\n1518\t\n1519\t- Geometry: line speed 80 (city); curve R 800 R at 12,400–12,800; signals SG-S 12,170, B401 13,000, DG-H 13,500, DG-S 13,770, B403 14,400,\n1520\t  KO-H 15,100; curve R 1000 L at 14,000; horn board 14,350 (park path).\n1521\t- **Rival** Sky Liner on x +7:\n1522\t  - it leaves Shotengai 5 s after us;\n1523\t  - runs level with us to 12,800 (its driver Ren on the radio);\n1524\t  - pulls ahead at 95;\n1525\t  - passes Daigaku-mae;\n1526\t  - waits at Koen, where it arrives first and stands beside our platform (its driver waves).\n1527\t- **Door rush** at Daigaku-mae (+8 s). **Glare** from 13,750 to 14,600. Crowd level 3 at every stop. `oncoming` on x +14 at 14,800.\n1528\t- Teaches: train length and stop markers, making up lost time without speeding, staying calm beside a faster train.\n1529\t\n1530\t**S5 · THE LAST HALO.** 23:10 night, fog patches, `h8000-6`, Sakura-Koen → Hoshimi-dai → Kawasemi → Akari Central.\n1531\t\n1532\t| stop | arr | dep |\n1533\t|---|---|---|\n1534\t| SAKURA-KOEN | — | 23:10:00 |\n1535\t| HOSHIMI-DAI | 23:12:15 | 23:12:35 |\n1536\t| KAWASEMI | 23:14:35 | 23:14:55 |\n1537\t| AKARI CENTRAL | 23:17:05 | — |\n1538\t\n1539\t- Geometry:\n1540\t  - quad ends at 15,600; curve R 600 R at 15,700–16,100;\n1541\t  - climb 15‰ from 16,100 to 16,900, with **fog 16,200–16,800**;\n1542\t  - Hoshimi-dai at 17,100;\n1543\t  - descent 12‰ from 17,500 to 18,200; curve R 700 L at 17,800–18,100 (limit 70);\n1544\t  - Kawasemi at 18,800;\n1545\t  - horn board 19,100; river bridge 19,200–19,500;\n1546\t  - downtown from 19,900; overpass at 20,150; limit 45 at 20,200 (points);\n1547\t  - **home signal AK-H at 20,350 shows YY** (restricted 25 into the terminal);\n1548\t  - Akari Central at 20,600.\n1549\t- Events: `fog`; `oncoming` last train at 19,000 with **flash** (answer with the horn: +2 s); the platform finale (crowd and staff line up, everyone\n1550\t  bows).\n1551\t- Then the **ending** (§4.26).\n1552\t- Teaches: night driving, fog and trusting signals, the YY aspect; the story's close.\n1553\t\n1554\t**PR · PARALLEL RUN** (Duel and hub; also in Free Run). 12:00 day, clear, `h8000-6`, Shotengai → Daigaku-mae → Sakura-Koen on the quad track. All\n1555\tfour tracks run clockwise (\"the Drivers' Festival\").\n1556\t\n1557\t| stop | arr | dep |\n1558\t|---|---|---|\n1559\t| SHOTENGAI | — | 12:00:00 |\n1560\t| DAIGAKU-MAE | 12:01:55 | 12:02:15 |\n1561\t| SAKURA-KOEN | 12:04:05 | — |\n1562\t\n1563\t- Every track has its own signals, with identical block timing. No rival AI, door rush or glare.\n1564\t- In a session the score is the standings (higher wins). The round fits in 5 min with the card and results.\n1565\t\n1566\t### 5.4 Characters (Humanoid rigs for portraits and on-world figures; Blob for the mascot)\n1567\t\n1568\t| Character | Role | Look (`E.Humanoid` options) | Voice | Notes |\n1569\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n1570\t| **Tetsuo Hoshino** | Chief Instructor, 38 years, last day | `build:'heroic'`, navy coat uniform, cap with a gold badge (`hat:{style:'cap',color:'#1a2a4a'}`), grey hair, white moustache (drawn at the portrait), white gloves | hoshino | dry, proverbial; never quite praises |\n1571\t| **Mika Aoba** | your conductor | navy uniform, cap, ponytail, armband | mika | warm, exclamation marks |\n1572\t| **Haro-kun** | Halo Line mascot | `E.Blob({ R: 7, colors: white/cream, wings: true, feet: true, mouth: true })` plus a drawn gold halo ring and headlight-eyes | haro | title, tips, PERFECT, attract host, boot screen |\n1573\t| **Station Master Ota** | Akari Central | grey coat, red-banded cap | ota | S5 finale |\n1574\t| **Kota** | train-fan kid at Hanabatake | small (`size:.8`), yellow cap, backpack, camera | kota | waves at every stop |\n1575\t| **Grandma Fuji** | regular at Okiku-dera/Yuhi-zaka | kimono colours, bun hair, `hunch` | fuji | bows |\n1576\t| **Kenji** | salaryman, always late | suit, tie, briefcase | kenji | the S4 door rush |\n1577\t| **Ren Kurosawa** | Sky Liner driver | purple uniform, sunglasses | ren | cocky radio, friendly at the end |\n1578\t| **Sato** | old driver on the inner loop | like Hoshino, older | sato | the S5 headlight flash |\n1579\t| crowds, staff, workers | — | seeded outfits by zone; staff in navy with white gloves; workers in orange vests and helmets, the lookout with a flag | crowd | §4.10 |\n1580\t\n1581\t### 5.5 Writing style guide and script\n1582\t\n1583\t**Style** (after the source's tone):\n1584\t- Short, earnest sentences in railway vocabulary.\n1585\t- Announcements are formal, say the station name twice, and repeat formulas (\"The doors on the left side will open.\").\n1586\t- Calls are romaji with English subtitles.\n1587\t- The instructor is terse and proverbial and hides his warmth; the conductor is cheerful.\n1588\t- Arcade banners are 1–3 words in capitals.\n1589\t- Light comedy comes from Japanese railway earnestness, never from mocking it.\n1590\t- No line wraps past 3 rows at 320 px.\n1591\t\n1592\t**Banners:** PERFECT HALO! · GREAT! · GOOD · OK · SHORT · OVERRUN! · OVER THE MARK · ON TIME! · LATE +4 · EARLY · SMOOTH! · CALL! · HORN +1 · LIMIT! ·\n1593\tATS! · EMERGENCY · HAZARD AVOIDED · MISSED STOP · WRONG STOP · SIGNAL PASSED AT DANGER.\n1594\t\n1595\t**Announcer (pa):**\n1596\t- \"Thank you for riding the Halo Line. This is a local train for Kujira-bashi.\"\n1597\t- \"The next station is Hanabatake. Hanabatake. The doors on the left side will open.\"\n1598\t- \"This is a Rapid service. We will not stop at Todai-shita.\"\n1599\t- \"Okiku-dera. Okiku-dera. Festival visitors, please mind the gap.\"\n1600\t- \"The next station is Akari Central, the last stop. Thank you for riding the Halo Line today.\"\n1601\t\n1602\t**S0 (Hoshino):**\n1603\t- \"So. You're the new one.\"\n1604\t- \"Thirty-eight years I drove this ring. Not one second late. Today is my last day.\"\n1605\t- \"Your paperwork says you can drive. The rails don't read paperwork.\"\n1606\t- Steps:\n1607\t  1. \"Lever up: power. P1. Gently.\"\n1608\t  2. \"N. Let her coast.\"\n1609\t  3. \"Lever down: brake. Watch the needle, not your hand.\"\n1610\t  4. \"The yellow board. Put your nose on it.\"\n1611\t  5. \"Before you move, point at the signal and say it. Shuppatsu, shinko.\"\n1612\t  6. \"Forty is the limit. Forty is not a suggestion.\"\n1613\t  7. \"Near the stop, ease off to B1. The passengers' coffee will thank you.\"\n1614\t  8. \"That is the emergency brake. You will hate the day you need it.\"\n1615\t  9. \"Last mark. Inside one metre and I sign your card.\"\n1616\t- The pass: \"...Hmph. Signed. The 06:40 is waiting, Rookie.\"\n1617\t\n1618\t**S1:**\n1619\t- Mika: \"Good morning, Driver! Conductor Aoba, at the back. Call me Mika!\"\n1620\t- Hoshino: \"Arrive on the second. Early is not on time. Late is not on time.\"\n1621\t- Mika: \"Melody, doors, my buzzer, then she's all yours!\"\n1622\t- Kota (on the platform): \"Haro! Haro! Mister driver!\" Mika: \"Our biggest fan is here again.\"\n1623\t- Hoshino (at the horn board): \"The fishermen under the bridge like to know we're coming.\"\n1624\t\n1625\t**S2:**\n1626\t- Hoshino: \"Today, the old 3000. She's older than you. Her brakes think slowly. Ask early.\"\n1627\t- Mika: \"Umbrellas everywhere! The rails will be slippery!\"\n1628\t- Dispatcher: \"Halo 1015, freight ahead of you through the cliff tunnel. Expect restrictive signals.\"\n1629\t- Hoshino at Y: \"Yellow. Forty-five. Don't argue with yellow.\"\n1630\t- Mika on slip: \"Wheels spinning! Ease the power!\"\n1631\t- Hoshino passing: \"Tsuka. Good. Eyes forward.\"\n1632\t\n1633\t**S3:**\n1634\t- Mika: \"It's the Chrysanthemum Festival!\"\n1635\t- Hoshino: \"Up the hill it's easy to be slow. Down it, easy to be fast.\"\n1636\t- Hoshino at the workers: \"Horn. Now.\"\n1637\t- Mika at the obstruction: \"The crossing alarm! Something's on the tracks!\"\n1638\t- Afterwards: \"The takoyaki survived. So did we.\"\n1639\t- Fuji: \"Thank you, driver-san!\"\n1640\t\n1641\t**S4:**\n1642\t- Hoshino: \"Ten cars. Your marker is the 10, not the 6.\"\n1643\t- Ren: \"Evening, Halo Line! See you at Koen... if you can keep up!\"\n1644\t- Hoshino: \"Ignore him. He has his timetable. We have ours.\"\n1645\t- Kenji: \"Wait! Wait for me!\"\n1646\t- Mika: \"One moment please! Doors re-opening!\"\n1647\t- Hoshino: \"Eight seconds. Earn them back. Without speeding.\"\n1648\t- Hoshino in the glare: \"West sun. Squint if you must. Don't guess.\"\n1649\t\n1650\t**S5:**\n1651\t- Mika: \"Last train of the night... and Hoshino-san's last run.\"\n1652\t- Hoshino: \"Don't make it a ceremony. Drive it like any other train.\"\n1653\t- Hoshino in the fog: \"When you can't see, the signals see for you.\"\n1654\t- Hoshino at Sato's flash: \"That's Sato. Thirty years. He's flashing for me... Answer him.\""}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a6a22e8e-f9ad-4c1e-b19f-6f268b0ad619","uuid":"4ee80c93-74b1-486d-89bd-dde9abeb9cc5","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:34:15.036Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174801__xc8e150/work/PLAN.md","content":"| OKIKU-DERA | (dwell) | 14:00:00 |\n| YUHI-ZAKA | 14:02:40 | 14:03:00 |\n| SHOTENGAI | 14:05:30 | — |\n\n- Geometry:\n  - crossing X2 at 9,050 (normal);\n  - climb **25‰** from 9,200 to 10,300; curve R 600 R at 9,300–9,600; curve R 450 L at 9,900–10,200 (limit 60);\n  - horn board 9,450; **workers** with a slow order of 25 from 9,600 to 9,900 (lookout at 9,550);\n  - Yuhi-zaka at 10,450;\n  - descent **20‰** from 10,700 to 11,450; curve R 500 L at 10,900–11,200 (limit 55);\n  - **obstruction emitter at 11,150 for crossing X3 at 11,500** (the festival's takoyaki cart); horn board 11,400;\n  - viaduct from 11,700; Shotengai at 12,100.\n- Events: festival (crowd ×2, lanterns, taiko), `workers`, `obstruction` at X3 (clears 12 s after we stop), Grandma Fuji bows at Yuhi-zaka, `oncoming`\n  at 11,200.\n- Teaches: gradients both ways, a slow order and the horn for workers, an emergency stop, a festival crowd.\n\n**S4 · SUNSET RUSH.** 17:30 sunset, clear, **`h8000-10`** (10-car marker), Shotengai → Daigaku-mae → Sakura-Koen, quad track.\n\n| stop | arr | dep |\n|---|---|---|\n| SHOTENGAI | — | 17:30:00 |\n| DAIGAKU-MAE | 17:31:55 | 17:32:15 |\n| SAKURA-KOEN | 17:34:05 | — |\n\n- Geometry: line speed 80 (city); curve R 800 R at 12,400–12,800; signals SG-S 12,170, B401 13,000, DG-H 13,500, DG-S 13,770, B403 14,400,\n  KO-H 15,100; curve R 1000 L at 14,000; horn board 14,350 (park path).\n- **Rival** Sky Liner on x +7:\n  - it leaves Shotengai 5 s after us;\n  - runs level with us to 12,800 (its driver Ren on the radio);\n  - pulls ahead at 95;\n  - passes Daigaku-mae;\n  - waits at Koen, where it arrives first and stands beside our platform (its driver waves).\n- **Door rush** at Daigaku-mae (+8 s). **Glare** from 13,750 to 14,600. Crowd level 3 at every stop. `oncoming` on x +14 at 14,800.\n- Teaches: train length and stop markers, making up lost time without speeding, staying calm beside a faster train.\n\n**S5 · THE LAST HALO.** 23:10 night, fog patches, `h8000-6`, Sakura-Koen → Hoshimi-dai → Kawasemi → Akari Central.\n\n| stop | arr | dep |\n|---|---|---|\n| SAKURA-KOEN | — | 23:10:00 |\n| HOSHIMI-DAI | 23:12:15 | 23:12:35 |\n| KAWASEMI | 23:14:35 | 23:14:55 |\n| AKARI CENTRAL | 23:17:05 | — |\n\n- Geometry:\n  - quad ends at 15,600; curve R 600 R at 15,700–16,100;\n  - climb 15‰ from 16,100 to 16,900, with **fog 16,200–16,800**;\n  - Hoshimi-dai at 17,100;\n  - descent 12‰ from 17,500 to 18,200; curve R 700 L at 17,800–18,100 (limit 70);\n  - Kawasemi at 18,800;\n  - horn board 19,100; river bridge 19,200–19,500;\n  - downtown from 19,900; overpass at 20,150; limit 45 at 20,200 (points);\n  - **home signal AK-H at 20,350 shows YY** (restricted 25 into the terminal);\n  - Akari Central at 20,600.\n- Events: `fog`; `oncoming` last train at 19,000 with **flash** (answer with the horn: +2 s); the platform finale (crowd and staff line up, everyone\n  bows).\n- Then the **ending** (§4.26).\n- Teaches: night driving, fog and trusting signals, the YY aspect; the story's close.\n\n**PR · PARALLEL RUN** (Duel and hub; also in Free Run). 12:00 day, clear, `h8000-6`, Shotengai → Daigaku-mae → Sakura-Koen on the quad track. All\nfour tracks run clockwise (\"the Drivers' Festival\").\n\n| stop | arr | dep |\n|---|---|---|\n| SHOTENGAI | — | 12:00:00 |\n| DAIGAKU-MAE | 12:01:55 | 12:02:15 |\n| SAKURA-KOEN | 12:04:05 | — |\n\n- Every track has its own signals, with identical block timing. No rival AI, door rush or glare.\n- In a session the score is the standings (higher wins). The round fits in 5 min with the card and results.\n\n### 5.4 Characters (Humanoid rigs for portraits and on-world figures; Blob for the mascot)\n\n| Character | Role | Look (`E.Humanoid` options) | Voice | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **Tetsuo Hoshino** | Chief Instructor, 38 years, last day | `build:'heroic'`, navy coat uniform, cap with a gold badge (`hat:{style:'cap',color:'#1a2a4a'}`), grey hair, white moustache (drawn at the portrait), white gloves | hoshino | dry, proverbial; never quite praises |\n| **Mika Aoba** | your conductor | navy uniform, cap, ponytail, armband | mika | warm, exclamation marks |\n| **Haro-kun** | Halo Line mascot | `E.Blob({ R: 7, colors: white/cream, wings: true, feet: true, mouth: true })` plus a drawn gold halo ring and headlight-eyes | haro | title, tips, PERFECT, attract host, boot screen |\n| **Station Master Ota** | Akari Central | grey coat, red-banded cap | ota | S5 finale |\n| **Kota** | train-fan kid at Hanabatake | small (`size:.8`), yellow cap, backpack, camera | kota | waves at every stop |\n| **Grandma Fuji** | regular at Okiku-dera/Yuhi-zaka | kimono colours, bun hair, `hunch` | fuji | bows |\n| **Kenji** | salaryman, always late | suit, tie, briefcase | kenji | the S4 door rush |\n| **Ren Kurosawa** | Sky Liner driver | purple uniform, sunglasses | ren | cocky radio, friendly at the end |\n| **Sato** | old driver on the inner loop | like Hoshino, older | sato | the S5 headlight flash |\n| crowds, staff, workers | — | seeded outfits by zone; staff in navy with white gloves; workers in orange vests and helmets, the lookout with a flag | crowd | §4.10 |\n\n### 5.5 Writing style guide and script\n\n**Style** (after the source's tone):\n- Short, earnest sentences in railway vocabulary.\n- Announcements are formal, say the station name twice, and repeat formulas (\"The doors on the left side will open.\").\n- Calls are romaji with English subtitles.\n- The instructor is terse and proverbial and hides his warmth; the conductor is cheerful.\n- Arcade banners are 1–3 words in capitals.\n- Light comedy comes from Japanese railway earnestness, never from mocking it.\n- No line wraps past 3 rows at 320 px.\n\n**Banners:** PERFECT HALO! · GREAT! · GOOD · OK · SHORT · OVERRUN! · OVER THE MARK · ON TIME! · LATE +4 · EARLY · SMOOTH! · CALL! · HORN +1 · LIMIT! ·\nATS! · EMERGENCY · HAZARD AVOIDED · MISSED STOP · WRONG STOP · SIGNAL PASSED AT DANGER.\n\n**Announcer (pa):**\n- \"Thank you for riding the Halo Line. This is a local train for Kujira-bashi.\"\n- \"The next station is Hanabatake. Hanabatake. The doors on the left side will open.\"\n- \"This is a Rapid service. We will not stop at Todai-shita.\"\n- \"Okiku-dera. Okiku-dera. Festival visitors, please mind the gap.\"\n- \"The next station is Akari Central, the last stop. Thank you for riding the Halo Line today.\"\n\n**S0 (Hoshino):**\n- \"So. You're the new one.\"\n- \"Thirty-eight years I drove this ring. Not one second late. Today is my last day.\"\n- \"Your paperwork says you can drive. The rails don't read paperwork.\"\n- Steps:\n  1. \"Lever up: power. P1. Gently.\"\n  2. \"N. Let her coast.\"\n  3. \"Lever down: brake. Watch the needle, not your hand.\"\n  4. \"The yellow board. Put your nose on it.\"\n  5. \"Before you move, point at the signal and say it. Shuppatsu, shinko.\"\n  6. \"Forty is the limit. Forty is not a suggestion.\"\n  7. \"Near the stop, ease off to B1. The passengers' coffee will thank you.\"\n  8. \"That is the emergency brake. You will hate the day you need it.\"\n  9. \"Last mark. Inside one metre and I sign your card.\"\n- The pass: \"...Hmph. Signed. The 06:40 is waiting, Rookie.\"\n\n**S1:**\n- Mika: \"Good morning, Driver! Conductor Aoba, at the back. Call me Mika!\"\n- Hoshino: \"Arrive on the second. Early is not on time. Late is not on time.\"\n- Mika: \"Melody, doors, my buzzer, then she's all yours!\"\n- Kota (on the platform): \"Haro! Haro! Mister driver!\" Mika: \"Our biggest fan is here again.\"\n- Hoshino (at the horn board): \"The fishermen under the bridge like to know we're coming.\"\n\n**S2:**\n- Hoshino: \"Today, the old 3000. She's older than you. Her brakes think slowly. Ask early.\"\n- Mika: \"Umbrellas everywhere! The rails will be slippery!\"\n- Dispatcher: \"Halo 1015, freight ahead of you through the cliff tunnel. Expect restrictive signals.\"\n- Hoshino at Y: \"Yellow. Forty-five. Don't argue with yellow.\"\n- Mika on slip: \"Wheels spinning! Ease the power!\"\n- Hoshino passing: \"Tsuka. Good. Eyes forward.\"\n\n**S3:**\n- Mika: \"It's the Chrysanthemum Festival!\"\n- Hoshino: \"Up the hill it's easy to be slow. Down it, easy to be fast.\"\n- Hoshino at the workers: \"Horn. Now.\"\n- Mika at the obstruction: \"The crossing alarm! Something's on the tracks!\"\n- Afterwards: \"The takoyaki survived. So did we.\"\n- Fuji: \"Thank you, driver-san!\"\n\n**S4:**\n- Hoshino: \"Ten cars. Your marker is the 10, not the 6.\"\n- Ren: \"Evening, Halo Line! See you at Koen... if you can keep up!\"\n- Hoshino: \"Ignore him. He has his timetable. We have ours.\"\n- Kenji: \"Wait! Wait for me!\"\n- Mika: \"One moment please! Doors re-opening!\"\n- Hoshino: \"Eight seconds. Earn them back. Without speeding.\"\n- Hoshino in the glare: \"West sun. Squint if you must. Don't guess.\"\n\n**S5:**\n- Mika: \"Last train of the night... and Hoshino-san's last run.\"\n- Hoshino: \"Don't make it a ceremony. Drive it like any other train.\"\n- Hoshino in the fog: \"When you can't see, the signals see for you.\"\n- Hoshino at Sato's flash: \"That's Sato. Thirty years. He's flashing for me... Answer him.\"","numLines":160,"startLine":1495,"totalLines":1945}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01YJHEyKbQyZmFZbJGHkV3gN","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
