{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013HdCNUMqMeri5oBWTLEKjU","type":"tool_result","content":"1893\t1. `node tools/bundle.mjs` writes `../DenshaDeHalo-DenshaDeGo-<model>-<ts>.html`:\n1894\t   - `<meta charset=\"utf-8\">`, then the **unmodified** `session.js` `<script>` as the first script;\n1895\t   - then the hub meta tags (§4.23), the viewport and the `<title>Densha de Halo!</title>`;\n1896\t   - the engine's boot splash markup (`E.bootSplash('DENSHA DE HALO!')`);\n1897\t   - the canvas;\n1898\t   - then inline scripts: the engine (patched), rail.js, `src/*.js`.\n1899\t   - No harness files, no external URLs, no `alert`/`confirm`/`prompt`.\n1900\t2. `node test/run.mjs --browser --hub` passes **on the bundle**: 0 failed.\n1901\t3. Search the code for `TODO`, `FIXME`, `placeholder`, `lorem` and `stub`: nothing found.\n1902\t4. Every TASK.md item is present (the checklist below).\n1903\t5. **About & Credits** pages filled with: Source Information (Date, Source, Plan = `PLAN.md`, Genre and Perspective, Tech with versions, Art\n1904\t   Direction, Animation, Audio, Online, Testing, Research, Environment, Model, Usage), Testing Feedback (4 answers), Engine Feedback (6 answers),\n1905\t   Prompt Feedback (4 answers). Write \"unknown\" for anything you can't confirm. Put the same text in the chat reply.\n1906\t6. `exit-interview.json` beside the HTML, in exactly TASK.md's shape. Check that it parses (`node -e \"JSON.parse(require('fs').readFileSync('exit-interview.json','utf8'))\"`).\n1907\t   Suggested `aiHub` values, to adjust to what you built:\n1908\t   - name: \"Densha de Halo!\"\n1909\t   - tagline: \"Stop on the mark. Leave on the second.\"\n1910\t   - description: \"Drive the Halo Line, a loop railway around Akari City, from the first train at dawn to the last train at night: stop exactly\n1911\t     on the mark, keep the timetable to the second, and point and call every signal. Race up to three friends on the four-track Parallel Run.\"\n1912\t   - type: \"Game\"; genre: \"Simulation\"; source: \"Densha de Go!\"; series: \"Densha de Go!\"\n1913\t   - players: \"1–4\" (solo, local duel, sessions of 2–4)\n1914\t   - controls: \"Lever W/S or L2/R2 · Call E/✕ · Horn Space/□ · ATS Q/△ · EB Backspace/L1\"\n1915\t   - tags: [\"first-person\", \"vehicles\", \"arcade\", \"retro\", \"versus\", \"story\"]\n1916\t7. Source Information defaults to start from (make them true):\n1917\t   - Genre: \"Train driving simulation with arcade scoring\".\n1918\t   - Perspective: \"First-person cab view (pseudo-3D), with chase, platform and trackside cameras, a side-view stop cam and a ring map\".\n1919\t   - Tech: \"my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (full engine, handoff package) + custom rail.js renderer; AI Hub session client 1.4.0; vanilla JS; Node + Playwright 1.63.0 for tests\".\n1920\t   - Art: \"the engine's PS1-era pixel style; new code-drawn trains, cab, signals, stations and Japanese townscape; library props via E.shapeSprite\".\n1921\t   - Animation: \"engine Humanoid/Blob rigs with new bow/point/flag poses; code-tweened cab controls, gloved hand, doors, gates\".\n1922\t   - Audio: \"all procedural WebAudio: VVVF inverter, rail joints, brakes, horn, crossing bells, 12 departure melodies, chip music, Babble gibberish voices\".\n1923\t   - Online: \"AI Hub Session Protocol v1, ghost mode, 2–4 players\".\n1924\t   - Research: what you did, e.g. \"read the engine handoff docs and the AI Hub protocol; no web research\", or what you looked up.\n1925\t8. Delete scratch clones (`_src/`) and `test/.serve/`, and stop any servers you started.\n1926\t\n1927\t**TASK.md coverage checklist** (tick each in M9):\n1928\t- [ ] title by RNG (above)\n1929\t- [ ] genre and perspective chosen (§1)\n1930\t- [ ] single HTML plus dev folder (§3.2, §9)\n1931\t- [ ] built on the handoff engine, changes logged (§3.8)\n1932\t- [ ] the engine's style plus new source-flavoured art (§5.6)\n1933\t- [ ] the engine's animation plus new animations (§5.7)\n1934\t- [ ] all audio in code, gibberish voices (§4.16, §4.17)\n1935\t- [ ] AI Hub ghost sessions plus the game on its own plus local duel (§4.23, §4.24)\n1936\t- [ ] feature-complete demo that shows every mechanic (§5.3: each stage's \"Teaches\")\n1937\t- [ ] dev mode from the pause menu with live sliders and Reset (§4.21)\n1938\t- [ ] attract mode after 10 s; any input exits (§4.20)\n1939\t- [ ] source-like narrative tone (§5.5)\n1940\t- [ ] 10-foot, controller-first UI; native keyboard and mouse; mouse hover and click in menus and the world; prompts follow the last device;\n1941\t      PlayStation glyphs with an Xbox option; no dense screens (§2, §4.14, §4.15, §4.25, §4.26)\n1942\t- [ ] touch-only message, Settings button, attract still runs (§4.15)\n1943\t- [ ] no TODOs, placeholders or stubs (§9.3)\n1944\t- [ ] About/Credits plus the chat reply with Source Information and the three feedback sets (§9.5)\n1945\t- [ ] exit-interview.json valid (§9.6)\n1946\t- [ ] tests behind one command printing failures plus a one-line count, including the full scripted playthrough (§8)\n1947\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a6a22e8e-f9ad-4c1e-b19f-6f268b0ad619","uuid":"3fac3fc4-9389-467f-91f8-114c8f35fadc","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:34:35.254Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174801__xc8e150/work/PLAN.md","content":"1. `node tools/bundle.mjs` writes `../DenshaDeHalo-DenshaDeGo-<model>-<ts>.html`:\n   - `<meta charset=\"utf-8\">`, then the **unmodified** `session.js` `<script>` as the first script;\n   - then the hub meta tags (§4.23), the viewport and the `<title>Densha de Halo!</title>`;\n   - the engine's boot splash markup (`E.bootSplash('DENSHA DE HALO!')`);\n   - the canvas;\n   - then inline scripts: the engine (patched), rail.js, `src/*.js`.\n   - No harness files, no external URLs, no `alert`/`confirm`/`prompt`.\n2. `node test/run.mjs --browser --hub` passes **on the bundle**: 0 failed.\n3. Search the code for `TODO`, `FIXME`, `placeholder`, `lorem` and `stub`: nothing found.\n4. Every TASK.md item is present (the checklist below).\n5. **About & Credits** pages filled with: Source Information (Date, Source, Plan = `PLAN.md`, Genre and Perspective, Tech with versions, Art\n   Direction, Animation, Audio, Online, Testing, Research, Environment, Model, Usage), Testing Feedback (4 answers), Engine Feedback (6 answers),\n   Prompt Feedback (4 answers). Write \"unknown\" for anything you can't confirm. Put the same text in the chat reply.\n6. `exit-interview.json` beside the HTML, in exactly TASK.md's shape. Check that it parses (`node -e \"JSON.parse(require('fs').readFileSync('exit-interview.json','utf8'))\"`).\n   Suggested `aiHub` values, to adjust to what you built:\n   - name: \"Densha de Halo!\"\n   - tagline: \"Stop on the mark. Leave on the second.\"\n   - description: \"Drive the Halo Line, a loop railway around Akari City, from the first train at dawn to the last train at night: stop exactly\n     on the mark, keep the timetable to the second, and point and call every signal. Race up to three friends on the four-track Parallel Run.\"\n   - type: \"Game\"; genre: \"Simulation\"; source: \"Densha de Go!\"; series: \"Densha de Go!\"\n   - players: \"1–4\" (solo, local duel, sessions of 2–4)\n   - controls: \"Lever W/S or L2/R2 · Call E/✕ · Horn Space/□ · ATS Q/△ · EB Backspace/L1\"\n   - tags: [\"first-person\", \"vehicles\", \"arcade\", \"retro\", \"versus\", \"story\"]\n7. Source Information defaults to start from (make them true):\n   - Genre: \"Train driving simulation with arcade scoring\".\n   - Perspective: \"First-person cab view (pseudo-3D), with chase, platform and trackside cameras, a side-view stop cam and a ring map\".\n   - Tech: \"my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (full engine, handoff package) + custom rail.js renderer; AI Hub session client 1.4.0; vanilla JS; Node + Playwright 1.63.0 for tests\".\n   - Art: \"the engine's PS1-era pixel style; new code-drawn trains, cab, signals, stations and Japanese townscape; library props via E.shapeSprite\".\n   - Animation: \"engine Humanoid/Blob rigs with new bow/point/flag poses; code-tweened cab controls, gloved hand, doors, gates\".\n   - Audio: \"all procedural WebAudio: VVVF inverter, rail joints, brakes, horn, crossing bells, 12 departure melodies, chip music, Babble gibberish voices\".\n   - Online: \"AI Hub Session Protocol v1, ghost mode, 2–4 players\".\n   - Research: what you did, e.g. \"read the engine handoff docs and the AI Hub protocol; no web research\", or what you looked up.\n8. Delete scratch clones (`_src/`) and `test/.serve/`, and stop any servers you started.\n\n**TASK.md coverage checklist** (tick each in M9):\n- [ ] title by RNG (above)\n- [ ] genre and perspective chosen (§1)\n- [ ] single HTML plus dev folder (§3.2, §9)\n- [ ] built on the handoff engine, changes logged (§3.8)\n- [ ] the engine's style plus new source-flavoured art (§5.6)\n- [ ] the engine's animation plus new animations (§5.7)\n- [ ] all audio in code, gibberish voices (§4.16, §4.17)\n- [ ] AI Hub ghost sessions plus the game on its own plus local duel (§4.23, §4.24)\n- [ ] feature-complete demo that shows every mechanic (§5.3: each stage's \"Teaches\")\n- [ ] dev mode from the pause menu with live sliders and Reset (§4.21)\n- [ ] attract mode after 10 s; any input exits (§4.20)\n- [ ] source-like narrative tone (§5.5)\n- [ ] 10-foot, controller-first UI; native keyboard and mouse; mouse hover and click in menus and the world; prompts follow the last device;\n      PlayStation glyphs with an Xbox option; no dense screens (§2, §4.14, §4.15, §4.25, §4.26)\n- [ ] touch-only message, Settings button, attract still runs (§4.15)\n- [ ] no TODOs, placeholders or stubs (§9.3)\n- [ ] About/Credits plus the chat reply with Source Information and the three feedback sets (§9.5)\n- [ ] exit-interview.json valid (§9.6)\n- [ ] tests behind one command printing failures plus a one-line count, including the full scripted playthrough (§8)\n","numLines":55,"startLine":1893,"totalLines":1947}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_013HdCNUMqMeri5oBWTLEKjU","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
